# emission of the laid out machine form into masc, which encodes it into a
# mink object
#
# this is the last stage of a register machine. a function's blocks and
# instructions are handed to masc's instruction-level api in memory, one
# instruction at a time by the row it is and the operands it has, into the
# text section of one builder, and the builder hands back the object. mirl
# never encodes a byte and never writes an object file. the machine form text
# is the one text hand-over: a function read from it is the same function and
# emits the same object, and masc's listing of the result is for debugging.
#
# an instruction is handed over in the row selection chose for it, or in the
# first short form of that row the set's record states whose fixed registers
# allocation gave it and whose requirement the view admits, as x86's
# accumulator forms. selection chose the row before any register was known,
# and masc's reader takes the short form for the text of the long one, so the
# object reads back from its listing only in the short form.
#
# an instruction written alone goes through masc's trusted path: the stages
# before this one chose its row and values, so nothing is asked of them again
# and a wrong one is mirl's bug. a checked build reads each against its row
# here, and a sequence, whose forms its relocations fix, always is.
#
# a block is an anonymous label of the builder, and a function is a named one
# exposed as a function symbol of its linkage, in the section it states or,
# when it states none, the one nameless text section, at the larger of the
# target's function alignment and its own, sized by its range: an
# anonymous label placed after its last instruction, before any padding that
# follows, which masc measures it to once it has laid the section out. a
# global with an initial value is a named label exposed as a data symbol of
# its linkage and size, in the section it states or, when it states none, the
# one nameless section of the kind its facts pick, which mink names as the
# format names a section of that kind, at its alignment, and its initial
# value is its bytes and a datum for each address in it. a build that asks
# for functions or data apart places each function or global of that kind
# that states no section in a nameless section of its own, opened apart, for
# the linker's garbage collection, and a function's jump tables then share one
# section of their own. a section a symbol states is one section per name
# whatever the build asks. an instruction another names as a partner is a label of its own, so a pc-relative low part's relocation names
# its high part. an operand that names a symbol or a partner takes the fixup
# kind the set binds its relocation kind to, and a fixup whose relocation
# covers the instructions after it is written with them as one sequence, as
# the set's spans state. alignment and fill come from the target's code
# declaration.
#
# a jump table is laid out after its function, in the read-only section of
# the kind a constant holding addresses is placed in under the target's
# relocation model, at its entries' alignment: its label, which the jump's
# address names as a partner, then one absolute datum of the pointer's width
# per block it names, the block's label. the table emits nothing in the code,
# whose last instruction is the jump through it.
#
# an inline assembly block is handed to masc whole, each of its operands at
# the location allocation gave it, and masc encodes it at the builder's
# cursor as the assembler encodes the same text. a symbol its text names is
# the builder's label of that name, and once every unit and global is
# emitted, each such label nothing placed or exposed is the module's symbol
# of that name when it has one, else an undefined symbol of the object with
# default binding, as an ir declaration is.
#
# a function that requires constant time is a constant-time range of masc's
# builder, begun at its label and ended after its last instruction, which
# mink's object keeps in the order emitted for the walk of its bytes and the
# note the linker reads. a conditional branch of such a function that
# selection marked as declassifying is a declassify point of the walk before
# it on every register and flag it reads, and any other declassifying
# instruction one after it on each register and extent it writes, at a label
# placed before it, whose place the finished object states. each call such a
# function makes, and each jump to a function, a tail call, is a call site of
# the walk, at a label placed before the instruction or the sequence it is
# written in, with the function its own operands or its sequence's name, which
# the walk's call model is made from. each memory access of such a function's
# instruction whose metadata states what it reads or writes, secret with its
# secret mark or public with the public flag selection keeps only on the one
# access it expands (`mirl.ir.opcode.row.states_access`, `states_write` and
# `states_copy`, whose read and write are each an access), is
# an access of the walk, at a label placed before the instruction or the
# sequence it is written in and named as the walk names it: by the operand its
# row's effect states it through, by its position in the effect for one no
# operand names, or by its memory operand. an inline block states none.
#
# a function whose architecture masc states a starting frame for is a frame
# of masc's builder, begun at its label and ended after its last instruction,
# and each call frame fact the frame stage stated, a rule or an epilogue
# scope's mark, is handed to masc in order at its instruction: before it, or
# after it for a fact that follows it. a
# module whose debug table states a source file hands masc its files once and
# each change of source location along the laid out code as a location before
# the instruction it begins at, an instruction with no location stated as
# line 0, never as a neighbour's. the object masc makes then states the debug
# records from the variable ranges of each function, at labels placed before
# the instructions they begin and end at, and from the runs of code inlined at
# each site, which mink lowers to the format's debugging information.
#
# a function or global its linkage marks exported is a directive of mink's
# object, an export about the symbol the object holds for it, exporting it by
# that symbol's name, added once the object is made. mink says whether it is
# code or data from the symbol's kind, and no attribute of a pe export is
# stated.

use std.types.bool.bool;
use std.types.bool.false;
use std.types.bool.true;
use std.types.char.char;
use std.types.error.err;
use std.types.option.opt;
use std.types.result.res;
use std.types.size.usize;
use std.types.string.str;
use std.types.string.str_equals;
use std.types.string.str_len;
use std.types.view.View;

use std.allocator;
use std.collections.map;
use std.collections.natural;
use std.collections.slice.Slice;
use std.collections.vector;
use std.encoding.binary;

use masc.build;
use build_emit: masc.build.emit;
use masc.build.frame;
use build_label:   masc.build.label;
use build_refusal: masc.build.refusal;
use build_section: masc.build.section;
use build_state:   masc.build.state;
use masc.build.trait;
use masc.codec;
use masc.core.effect;
use masc.core.field;
use core_fixup: masc.core.fixup;
use core_form:  masc.core.form;
use masc.core.inst;
use masc.core.mode;
use mo: masc.core.operand;
use masc.core.query;
use rf: masc.core.register;
use masc.core.relax;
use rows:         masc.core.row;
use masc_set:     masc.core.set;
use core_state:   masc.core.state;
use mswitch:      masc.core.switch;
use masc_emit:    masc.emit;
use masc_cfi:     masc.emit.cfi;
use masc_line:    masc.emit.line;
use masc_listing: masc.emit.listing;
use masc_dialect: masc.format.dialect;
use masc_inline:  masc.inline;
use masc.walk;
use mink_fail: mink.base.fail;
use mink.base.fail.Fail;
use mink.base.intern.Name;
use mink_table: mink.base.table;
use mink.base.table.Id;
use arches: mink.catalog.arch;
use mink.catalog.format.Format;
use mink.format.registration;
use mink.format.registry;
use mink_lower:  mink.lower;
use mink_bridge: mink.model.bridge;
use mink.model.directive;
use mink_line: mink.model.line;
use mink.model.object;
use mink.model.reloc;
use mink.model.section;
use mink.model.symbol;

use mirl.base.fail.keep;
use mirl.base.slice;
use mirl.base.stats.Stats;
use mct: mirl.ct;
use mirl.ct.contract;
use mirl.debug.records;
use ia: mirl.ir.assembly;
use mirl.ir.attribute.Attribute;
use mirl.ir.attribute.Datum;
use debug_place:  mirl.ir.debug.place;
use debug_record: mirl.ir.debug.record;
use debug_table:  mirl.ir.debug.table;
use mirl.ir.function.FunctionData;
use mirl.ir.function.in_constant_time;
use mirl.ir.global.GlobalData;
use mirl.ir.id;
use mirl.ir.linkage;
use mirl.ir.linkage.Linkage;
use mirl.ir.metadata;
use mirl.ir.module;
use mirl.ir.module.Contents;
use mirl.ir.module.Module;
use type_calling: mirl.ir.type.calling;
use type_table:   mirl.ir.type.table;
use mirl.ir.type.table.DEFAULT_SPACE;
use mirl.machine.class.Physical;
use mirl.machine.emit.data;
use mirl.machine.emit.fixup;
use mirl.machine.emit.timed;
use mirl.machine.frame.record.Fact;
use mirl.machine.frame.record.Statement;
use mirl.machine.function;
use mirl.machine.function.Function;
use mirl.machine.inline.Inline;
use mirl.machine.instruction;
use mirl.machine.instruction.InstructionData;
use mirl.machine.instruction.Opcode;
use mirl.machine.isa.Short;
use mirl.machine.isa.Shorts;
use mirl.machine.layout.lay.Laid;
use mirl.machine.operand;
use mirl.machine.operand.Block;
use mirl.machine.operand.Instruction;
use mirl.machine.operand.Operand;
use mirl.machine.operand.Register;
use mirl.machine.pseudo;
use mirl.machine.range.Range;
use mirl.machine.range.Ranges;
use mirl.target.abi.call;
use mirl.target.abi.convention;
use mirl.target.abi.convention.Bridging;
use mirl.target.abi.convention.Convention;
use mirl.target.abi.convention.Unadmitted;
use mirl.target.address;
use mirl.target.address.Addresses;
use mirl.target.build.Build;
use mirl.target.capability.Align;
use mirl.target.capability.Extent;
use mirl.target.capability.Fill;
use mirl.target.layout;
use mirl.target.layout.Layout;
use mirl.target.options.Apart;
use mirl.target.record;
use mirl.target.record.Target;
use mirl.target.register.schema;

# one function to hand over
# ---
# function: the symbol of the module it is the code of
# context:  the context its code was made under, the build's or the one its
#           extensions past the build's open, which it is handed over under
# code:     the function, allocated, framed and laid out
# laid:     the order its blocks are emitted in
# facts:    the call frame facts of its frame, at its instructions
# ranges:   where its variables are over its code, nil for nowhere
pub rec Unit {
    function: id.Function;
    context:  *core_state.Context;
    code:     *Function;
    laid:     *Laid;
    facts:    Slice[Fact];
    ranges:   *Ranges;
}

# an instruction that was not handed over, and where
# ---
# function: the function it is in
# at:       the instruction
# operand:  the operand position, NO_OPERAND for the instruction as a whole
# location: the source location the instruction was built for, none for none
pub rec At {
    function: id.Function;
    at:       Instruction;
    operand:  u32;
    location: opt[debug_record.Location];
}

# an inline assembly block masc refused to encode with its operands placed
# ---
# at:      the block
# message: masc's reason
pub rec Encoded {
    at:      At;
    message: str;
}

# a global whose initial value the module refused a read of
# ---
# global: the global
# error:  the module's refusal
pub rec Valued {
    global: id.Global;
    error:  module.Error;
}

# a global the data layout gives its type or a part of its initial value no
# extent
# ---
# global: the global
# error:  the layout's refusal
pub rec Sized {
    global: id.Global;
    error:  record.Error;
}

# a relocation the object's format does not map for the architecture, as masc refuses it
# ---
# symbol:  the function or global it aims at, none for a label the module does not name, as a block or a marker
# refusal: masc's refusal, whose object failure names the relocation kind and the format
pub rec Unmapped {
    symbol:  opt[id.Symbol];
    refusal: build_refusal.Refusal;
}

# what masc refused to list of the object, and the function or global it is about
# ---
# symbol:  the function or global the refusal's label names, or else the one
#          placed last at or before where it was found in its section, none
#          for a refusal of the object as a whole or of a place no symbol
#          of the module comes before
# refusal: masc's refusal, whose message names the construct the listing has no form of
pub rec Unlisted {
    symbol:  opt[id.Symbol];
    refusal: masc_listing.Refusal;
}

# a function or global the module marks exported that the object does not export
# ---
# symbol:  the function or global
# failure: mink's refusal of the export directive, none when the object holds no symbol of it
pub rec Unexported {
    symbol:  id.Symbol;
    failure: opt[Fail];
}

# why the object was not made
# ---
# alloc:      the allocator refused storage
# symbol:     a unit or an operand names a symbol the module does not have
# convention: the target's calling convention is not stated, so the psABI row its objects follow is not
# abi:        the convention leaves its psABI row unstated, or names one mink's catalog has not for the architecture
# fill:       the target's code fill is not one byte repeated, which masc's alignment takes, or is none where code is aligned
# builder:    masc refused
# unmapped:   the object's format maps no relocation of a kind the object needs
# section:    a function or global names a section another function or
#             global names with another kind
# dialect:    masc states no assembly dialect of the format, which the listing is written in
# listing:    masc refused to list the object it made, naming the construct and the symbol it is about
# debug:      the module's debug records were not stated on the object
# lowering:   mink states no registration of the object's format, whose lowering the debug records are stated for
# export:     the object refused to export a function or global the module marks exported
# pseudo:     an instruction holding a pseudo-instruction or loop no stage
#             expanded, which encodes to nothing
# unplaced:   an operand naming a virtual register or a frame slot, which
#             allocation and the frame replace
# cell:       an operand naming a location of a memory-backed class, which no
#             register machine holds in an object
# shape:      an operand of a kind its position does not take, an id
#             position given anything but a system register, or lists
#             holding more members than an instruction keeps room for
# unbound:    an operand of a relocation kind the set binds no fixup kind to
# ambiguous:  an operand of a relocation kind the set binds several fixup
#             kinds to, none the operand's own
# label:      a label two instructions hold, or inside a sequence, or a
#             partner naming a label no instruction holds
# span:       a relocation covering more instructions than the block has
#             after it
# fact:       a call frame fact at no instruction, or at one layout took out
#             of a block it kept
# table:      a jump table on a target that states no address model or no
#             pointer, so neither its section nor its entries' width is stated
# inline:     masc refused to encode an inline assembly block with its
#             operands placed
# contents:   the module refused a read of a global's initial value
# model:      a global whose initial value holds an address on a target that
#             states no address model
# layout:     the data layout gives a global's type or a part of its initial
#             value no extent
# width:      an address in a global's initial value is wider than any datum
#             masc relocates
# declassify: a declassifying instruction of a function that requires constant
#             time that leaves no declassify point of its own: one that
#             writes no register or extent a point names, is written in a
#             sequence, or encodes to no byte
pub tag Error: u8 {
    alloc:      allocator.Error;
    symbol:     module.Error;
    convention: call.Error;
    abi;
    fill;
    builder:    build_refusal.Refusal;
    unmapped:   Unmapped;
    section:    id.Symbol;
    dialect:    *Format;
    listing:    Unlisted;
    debug:      records.Error;
    lowering:   Fail;
    export:     Unexported;
    pseudo:     At;
    unplaced:   At;
    cell:       At;
    shape:      At;
    unbound:    At;
    ambiguous:  At;
    label:      At;
    span:       At;
    fact:       At;
    table:      At;
    inline:     Encoded;
    contents:   Valued;
    model:      id.Global;
    layout:     Sized;
    width:      id.Global;
    declassify: At;
}

# the operand an instruction as a whole is refused at
pub val NO_OPERAND: u32 = instruction.NO_OPERAND;

# a section the builder has opened
# ---
# section: the builder's section
# kind:    the role it plays
rec Opened {
    section: build_state.Section;
    kind:    *section.Kind;
}

# what one emission reads and changes
# ---
# a:         the allocator
# m:         the module, whose symbols the operands name
# opened:    the target's build
# t:         the target
# l:         the layout of the module's types for the target
# order:     the architecture's byte order
# b:         the builder
# x:         the set's fixup kinds by relocation kind
# functions: the label of each function of the module, none until it is named
# ends:      the label ending each unit's function, by the unit's position
# emitters:  the position of the unit that emits each function of the module, none for one no unit emits
# globals:   the label of each global of the module, none until it is named
# sections:  each section opened with a name the module states, by its name
# kinds:     the one nameless section of each kind opened, by its kind, re-entered by its handle since it has no name
# apart:     which symbols the build asks to place each in a section of its own
# fill:      the byte code is padded with, none when code is not padded
# function:  the alignment of a function's entry, none when it has none
# framed:    whether masc states a starting frame for the architecture, so each function is a frame
# lines:     the line facts handed to masc, valid while the builder is
# stated:    whether the module states source files, so its code carries line facts
# sourced:   the function and the source location of each line fact, in the order handed to masc
# spans:     where every variable is, over the labels of every unit
# runs:      the code inlined at each site, over the labels of every unit
# programs:  each unit's first span and run and their counts
# named:     the named labels the encodes of inline blocks made
# pending:   each declassify point, at the label before its branch
# calling:   each call site, at the label before what it is written in
# fixing:    each symbolic operand of a function that requires constant time, at the label before what it is written in
# stating:   each stated memory access of a function that requires constant time, at the label before what it is in
# marking:   each instruction of a function that requires constant time the walk takes a fact of beyond its row, at the
#            label before what it is in
# seeding:   each register an instruction of a function that requires constant time leaves a declared secret in, at the
#            label before what it is in
# shorts:    the rows an instruction is handed over in once its registers are allocated
# steps:     the instructions of the sequence being written, kept here so no write sets out room for its longest
# listed:    the members of their lists
# refusal:   why the emission stopped: what every step past the public entry points at, since an error passed by value
#            on each instruction's way through would cost more than writing the instruction
rec Emitter {
    a:         *allocator.Allocator;
    m:         *Module;
    opened:    *Build;
    t:         *Target;
    l:         Layout;
    order:     binary.Order;
    b:         *build_state.Builder;
    x:         *fixup.Index;
    functions: vector.Vector[opt[build_state.Label]];
    ends:      vector.Vector[build_state.Label];
    emitters:  vector.Vector[opt[u32]];
    globals:   vector.Vector[opt[build_state.Label]];
    sections:  map.MapBy[View, Opened];
    kinds:     map.MapBy[*section.Kind, build_state.Section];
    apart:     Apart;
    fill:      opt[u8];
    function:  opt[u64];
    framed:    bool;
    lines:     masc_line.Lines;
    stated:    bool;
    sourced:   vector.Vector[Sourced];
    spans:     vector.Vector[records.Span];
    runs:      vector.Vector[records.Run];
    programs:  vector.Vector[Program];
    named:     vector.Vector[build_state.Label];
    pending:   vector.Vector[Pending];
    calling:   vector.Vector[Calling];
    fixing:    vector.Vector[Fixing];
    stating:   vector.Vector[Stating];
    seeding:   vector.Vector[Seeding];
    marking:   vector.Vector[Marking];
    shorts:    Shorts;
    bridging:  opt[*Bridging];
    default:   *Convention;
    routine:   opt[str];
    plain:     vector.Vector[opt[build_state.Label]];
    steps:     [relax.MAX_STEPS]masc_emit.Instruction;
    listed:    [ROOM]mo.Value;
    refusal:   Error;
}

# what a line fact handed to masc was stated for
# ---
# function: the function whose code it begins a run of
# location: the source location of the run, none for an instruction that states none
rec Sourced {
    function: id.Function;
    location: opt[debug_record.Location];
}

# a declassify point at a label not yet placed
# ---
# function: the function
# label:    the label before its instruction
# side:     before for a branch reading the place as public, after for a copy writing it
# place:    the place
# end:      the label after its instruction, placed once the instruction is written
rec Pending {
    function: id.Function;
    label:    build_state.Label;
    side:     walk.Side;
    place:    walk.Place;
    end:      opt[build_state.Label];
}

# a call site at a label not yet placed
# ---
# function:    the function making the call
# label:       the label before the instruction or the sequence the call is written in
# instruction: the call
# tail:        it is a jump to a function, a tail call
# callee:      the function the call or its sequence names, none for one it reaches through a register
# steps:       how many instructions were written from the label, the call among them
rec Calling {
    function:    id.Function;
    label:       build_state.Label;
    instruction: Instruction;
    tail:        bool;
    callee:      opt[id.Function];
    steps:       u32;
}

# a symbolic operand of a function that requires constant time, its label not yet placed
# ---
# function: the function
# label:    the label before the instruction or the sequence it is written in
# step:     which instruction of that sequence it fills
# operand:  the operand it fills
# fixup:    the fixup kind it is applied as
# symbol:   the function or global it names, none for a low part naming its partner
# addend:   what it adds to the symbol
# partner:  the label of the instruction whose high part a low part takes, none for any other
rec Fixing {
    function: id.Function;
    label:    build_state.Label;
    step:     u32;
    operand:  u8;
    fixup:    mo.FixupKind;
    symbol:   opt[id.Symbol];
    addend:   i64;
    partner:  opt[build_state.Label];
}

# a symbolic operand written into the instruction being handed over, before the label of what it is written in is
# known to it
# ---
# at:      the instruction
# operand: the operand it fills
# fixup:   the fixup kind it is applied as
# symbol:  the function or global it names, none for a low part naming its partner
# addend:  what it adds to the symbol
# partner: the label of the instruction whose high part a low part takes, none for any other
rec Noted {
    at:      Instruction;
    operand: u8;
    fixup:   mo.FixupKind;
    symbol:  opt[id.Symbol];
    addend:  i64;
    partner: opt[build_state.Label];
}

# a memory access of a function that requires constant time whose secrecy its instruction states, its label not yet
# placed
# ---
# function: the function
# label:    the label before the instruction or the sequence it is written in
# step:     which instruction of that sequence makes it
# access:   the access, as the walk names it
# secrecy:  whether it states what it reads, secret or public
# secret:   whether what it reads may hold a secret
# extent:   the frame extent it states, length 0 for none
rec Stating {
    function: id.Function;
    label:    build_state.Label;
    step:     u32;
    access:   walk.Accessor;
    secrecy:  bool;
    secret:   bool;
    extent:   metadata.Extent;
}

# an instruction the walk takes a fact of beyond its row, at the label before what it is written in
# ---
# function: the function
# label:    where the instruction or the sequence it is written in starts
# step:     which instruction of that sequence it is, an inline block's counted one by one
# fact:     the fact
rec Marking {
    function: id.Function;
    label:    build_state.Label;
    step:     u32;
    fact:     timed.Fact;
}

# a stated memory access of the instruction being handed over, before the label of what it is written in is known to it
# ---
# at:      the instruction
# access:  the access, as the walk names it
# secrecy: whether it states what it reads, secret or public
# secret:  whether what it reads may hold a secret
# extent:  the frame extent it states, length 0 for none
rec Stated {
    at:      Instruction;
    access:  walk.Accessor;
    secrecy: bool;
    secret:  bool;
    extent:  metadata.Extent;
}

# a register an instruction leaves a declared secret in, at the label before what it is written in
# ---
# function: the function
# label:    where the instruction or the sequence it is written in starts
# step:     which instruction of that sequence it is, 0 for its first or one written alone
# register: the register
rec Seeding {
    function: id.Function;
    label:    build_state.Label;
    step:     u32;
    register: rf.Id;
}

# a register the instruction being handed over leaves a declared secret in, before the label of what it is written in
# is known to it
# ---
# at:       the instruction
# register: the register
rec Declared {
    at:       Instruction;
    register: rf.Id;
}

# where one unit's spans and runs are among the emission's
# ---
# function: the function
# start:    its label
# end:      the label after its last instruction
# spans:    its first span
# span:     how many spans it has
# runs:     its first run
# run:      how many runs it has
rec Program {
    function: id.Function;
    start:    build_state.Label;
    end:      build_state.Label;
    spans:    usize;
    span:     usize;
    runs:     usize;
    run:      usize;
}

# a label placed before an instruction a range begins or ends at, or at its
# block's end when layout left the instruction in no block
# ---
# label:   the label
# block:   the block the instruction is in
# defined: whether it is placed yet
rec Mark {
    label:   build_state.Label;
    block:   u32;
    defined: bool;
}

# what one function emits against
# ---
# e:      the emission
# u:      the function
# code:   the section its code is placed in
# blocks: the label of each block
# marks:  the label of each instruction a partner operand names, by the number the function gives it
# facts:  per instruction, its first call frame fact, NONE for none
# next:   per fact, the next fact at its instruction, NONE after the last
# given:  per fact, whether it was handed to masc
# laid:   per block, whether layout left it in the order it emits
# gone:   per instruction, whether it is in a block layout dropped, so emits
#         nothing, and nothing stated at it is due
# ranged: the label before each instruction a range begins or ends at, by its id
# ends:   the label at the end of each laid out block a range runs to the end of
# site:   the site the code being emitted was inlined at, none for none
# run:    the label the current run of inlined code began at
# at:     the source location last stated, none for none
# spoke:  whether a location was stated for the unit yet
# tables: the jump tables of the unit, laid out after its code
# noted:  the symbolic operands of the instructions being written, for a unit that requires constant time
# stated: the stated memory accesses of the instructions being written, for a unit that requires constant time
# seeded: the registers the instructions being written leave a declared secret in, for a unit that requires constant time
# uses:   the instructions of the inline block being written that name an operand, for a unit that requires constant time
# steps:  how many instructions the inline block being written wrote, for a unit that requires constant time
# switch: the rows of the timing switch the function's set states, none where it states none
# timed:  the function requires constant time
rec Body {
    e:      *Emitter;
    u:      Unit;
    code:   build_state.Section;
    blocks: vector.Vector[build_state.Label];
    marks:  map.Map[u32, build_state.Label];
    facts:  vector.Vector[u32];
    next:   vector.Vector[u32];
    given:  vector.Vector[bool];
    laid:   vector.Vector[bool];
    gone:   vector.Vector[bool];
    ranged: map.Map[u32, Mark];
    ends:   vector.Vector[opt[build_state.Label]];
    site:   opt[debug_record.Site];
    run:    build_state.Label;
    at:     opt[debug_record.Location];
    spoke:  bool;
    tables: vector.Vector[Instruction];
    noted:  vector.Vector[Noted];
    stated: vector.Vector[Stated];
    seeded: vector.Vector[Declared];
    uses:   vector.Vector[masc_inline.Use];
    steps:  u32;
    switch: opt[mct.Switching];
    timed:  bool;
}

val NONE: u32 = 0xffffffff;

# why an inline block of a function that requires constant time is refused when a data directive stops its encode's
# count of the instructions it wrote, which the walk tells the block's apart from the function's own by
val UNCOUNTED: str = "data directives are not allowed in the asm of a function that requires constant time, whose check tells a block's instructions apart by counting them";

fun site(b: *Body, at: Instruction, operand: u32) At {
    ret At{function: b.u.function, at: at, operand: operand, location: function.location(b.u.code, at)};
}

# stop the emission for `why`, kept on it, which the public entry hands back
fun stop(e: *Emitter, why: Error) *Error {
    e.refusal = why;
    ret ?e.refusal;
}

fun builder(e: *Emitter, r: err[build_refusal.Refusal]) err[*Error] {
    if (sel r.err) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.builder{r.err})}; }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# why masc refused to finish the object: a relocation the format does not map, named by the symbol it aims at, or
# anything else masc refuses
fun finish_refused(e: *Emitter, r: build_refusal.Refusal) Error {
    if (!str_equals(r.message, build_refusal.NO_RELOCATION)) { ret Error.builder{r}; }
    ret Error.unmapped{Unmapped{symbol: aimed_at(e, r.label), refusal: r}};
}

# the function or global whose label is `label`, none for a label the module does not name
fun aimed_at(e: *Emitter, label: u32) opt[id.Symbol] {
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < e.functions.len) {
        val f: opt[build_state.Label] = e.functions.data[i];
        if (sel f.some && f.some == label) { ret opt[id.Symbol].some{id.Symbol.function{(i::u32)}}; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < e.globals.len) {
        val g: opt[build_state.Label] = e.globals.data[i];
        if (sel g.some && g.some == label) { ret opt[id.Symbol].some{id.Symbol.global{(i::u32)}}; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret opt[id.Symbol].none{};
}

# why masc refused to list the object, named by the function or global it is about
fun unlisted(e: *Emitter, r: masc_listing.Refusal) Error {
    if (r.label != mo.NO_SYMBOL) { ret Error.listing{Unlisted{symbol: aimed_at(e, r.label), refusal: r}}; }
    ret Error.listing{Unlisted{symbol: placed_before(e, r.failure.at), refusal: r}};
}

# the function or global placed last at or before where `failed` points in its section, none for none
fun placed_before(e: *Emitter, failed: mink_fail.Location) opt[id.Symbol] {
    var found: opt[id.Symbol] = opt[id.Symbol].none{};
    if (!failed.indexed) { ret found; }
    var best: u64   = 0;
    var i:    usize = 0;
    for (i < e.functions.len + e.globals.len) {
        var l:      opt[build_state.Label] = opt[build_state.Label].none{};
        var symbol: id.Symbol;
        if (i < e.functions.len) {
            l      = e.functions.data[i];
            symbol = id.Symbol.function{(i::u32)};
        }
        or {
            l      = e.globals.data[i - e.functions.len];
            symbol = id.Symbol.global{((i - e.functions.len)::u32)};
        }
        if (sel l.some) {
            val at: opt[object.Place] = build.place_of(e.b, l.some);
            if (sel at.some) {
                val p: object.Place = at.some;
                if (p.section.index::u64 == failed.index && p.offset <= failed.offset && p.offset >= best) {
                    found = opt[id.Symbol].some{symbol};
                    best  = p.offset;
                }
            }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret found;
}

fun alloc(e: *Emitter, r: res[usize, allocator.Error]) err[*Error] {
    if (sel r.err) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.alloc{r.err})}; }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# bytes that carry no terminator, copied with one, the caller's to give back with `unterminated`
fun terminated(e: *Emitter, v: View) res[*u8, *Error] {
    val copy: res[*u8, allocator.Error] = allocator.allocate[u8](e.a, v.len + 1);
    if (sel copy.err) { ret res[*u8, *Error].err{stop(e, Error.alloc{copy.err})}; }
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < v.len) {
        copy.ok[i] = v.data[i];
        i          = i + 1;
    }
    copy.ok[v.len] = 0;
    ret res[*u8, *Error].ok{copy.ok};
}

fun unterminated(e: *Emitter, p: *u8, v: View) {
    allocator.deallocate[u8](e.a, p, v.len + 1);
}

# a label named by bytes the module declares nothing by, as a decorated spelling, interned in the builder's object
fun named(e: *Emitter, v: View) res[build_state.Label, *Error] {
    val n: res[Id[Name], Fail] = object.name(build.output(e.b), v.data::*u8, v.len);
    if (sel n.err) { ret res[build_state.Label, *Error].err{stop(e, Error.alloc{interned(n.err)})}; }
    ret handled(e, n.ok);
}

# the allocator's refusal a refusal to intern a name carries, which can be no other
fun interned(f: Fail) allocator.Error {
    val c: mink_fail.Cause = f.cause;
    if (sel c.refused) { ret c.refused; }
    ret allocator.Error.exhausted{};
}

# the label of a function by its decorated spelling where it has one, else by its handle `n`
fun declared_label(e: *Emitter, marked: bool, spelling: View, n: Id[Name]) res[build_state.Label, *Error] {
    if (marked) { ret named(e, spelling); }
    ret handled(e, n);
}

# the label of a function or global the module declares by the handle `n`, which names the same bytes in the builder's
# object, as the module lent it its names
fun handled(e: *Emitter, n: Id[Name]) res[build_state.Label, *Error] {
    val made: res[build_state.Label, build_refusal.Refusal] = build_label.label_of(e.b, n);
    if (sel made.err) { ret res[build_state.Label, *Error].err{stop(e, Error.builder{made.err})}; }
    ret res[build_state.Label, *Error].ok{made.ok};
}

# how the object shows a symbol of the module: its linkage's rows, of a kind,
# with its size, a count of bytes or a range masc measures once laid out
fun exposure(l: Linkage, kind: *symbol.Kind, size: build_state.Size) build_state.Exposure {
    ret build_state.Exposure{binding: l.binding, visibility: l.visibility, kind: kind, size: size};
}

# make label `l` the symbol `shows` states, but a local one in the dialect's private spelling, as elf's `.L`,
# which is local by being no symbol
fun expose(e: *Emitter, l: build_state.Label, shows: build_state.Exposure) err[build_refusal.Refusal] {
    if (shows.binding == ?symbol.LOCAL && build_label.private_label(e.b, l)) { ret err[build_refusal.Refusal].ok{}; }
    ret build_label.expose(e.b, l, shows);
}

# the name native code reaches a function by, written to `out`, where the
# target's default row bridges to another convention's code: a function of
# the default row, but the routine its frames call, named as the bridge
# decorates it. false for a function named as it is
fun decorated(e: *Emitter, data: *FunctionData, out: *vector.Vector[u8]) res[bool, *Error] {
    val b: opt[*Bridging] = e.bridging;
    if (sel b.none) { ret res[bool, *Error].ok{false}; }
    val s: res[type_table.Function, type_table.Error] = type_table.signature(?e.m.types, data.signature);
    if (sel s.err) { ret res[bool, *Error].err{stop(e, Error.symbol{module.Error.types{s.err}})}; }
    val k: opt[type_calling.Calling] = s.ok.convention;
    if (sel k.some && !convention.names(e.default, k.some)) { ret res[bool, *Error].ok{false}; }
    val routine: opt[str] = e.routine;
    val name:    View     = module.name_of(e.m, data.name);
    if (sel routine.some && slice.same_view(name, View{data: routine.some, len: str_len(routine.some)})) { ret res[bool, *Error].ok{false}; }
    val written: res[bool, allocator.Error] = b.some.decorate(name, out);
    if (sel written.err) { ret res[bool, *Error].err{stop(e, Error.alloc{written.err})}; }
    ret res[bool, *Error].ok{written.ok};
}

# the label of the guest exit thunk the module defines for a function of a
# decorated name, none where it defines none
fun guest_of(e: *Emitter, name: View) res[opt[build_state.Label], *Error] {
    val b: opt[*Bridging] = e.bridging;
    if (sel b.none) { ret res[opt[build_state.Label], *Error].ok{opt[build_state.Label].none{}}; }
    var spelled: vector.Vector[u8] = vector.init[u8](e.a);
    fin { vector.dnit[u8](?spelled); }
    val written: res[bool, allocator.Error] = b.some.guest(name, ?spelled);
    if (sel written.err) { ret res[opt[build_state.Label], *Error].err{stop(e, Error.alloc{written.err})}; }
    if (!written.ok)     { ret res[opt[build_state.Label], *Error].ok{opt[build_state.Label].none{}}; }
    val found: opt[id.Symbol] = module.find(e.m, View{data: spelled.data::*char, len: spelled.len});
    if (sel found.some) {
        val s: id.Symbol = found.some;
        if (sel s.function) {
            val l: res[build_state.Label, *Error] = function_label(e, s.function);
            if (sel l.err) { ret res[opt[build_state.Label], *Error].err{l.err}; }
            ret res[opt[build_state.Label], *Error].ok{opt[build_state.Label].some{l.ok}};
        }
    }
    ret res[opt[build_state.Label], *Error].ok{opt[build_state.Label].none{}};
}

# a weak external of a name that `target` stands in for unless the link
# defines the name otherwise, as an arm64ec name the other convention's code
# reaches stands for the native one (`.weak_anti_dep`)
fun anti_dependency(e: *Emitter, name: View, target: build_state.Label) res[build_state.Label, *Error] {
    val l: res[build_state.Label, *Error] = named(e, name);
    if (sel l.err) { ret l; }
    val shown: err[*Error] = builder(e, build_label.expose(e.b, l.ok, build_state.Exposure{binding: ?symbol.WEAKLY, visibility: ?symbol.DEFAULT, kind: ?symbol.FUNCTION, size: build_state.Size.none{}}));
    if (sel shown.err) { ret res[build_state.Label, *Error].err{shown.err}; }
    val fell: err[*Error] = builder(e, build_label.fall_back(e.b, l.ok, target, ?symbol.ANTI_DEPENDENCY));
    if (sel fell.err) { ret res[build_state.Label, *Error].err{fell.err}; }
    ret l;
}

# the label of a function of the module, a function symbol of the object made
# when it is first named, sized from its label to its end when a unit emits it.
# where the default row bridges, a function native code reaches by a name of
# its own takes that name ("arm64ec function name decoration"), and the name
# the other convention's code reaches it by is a label of its own: for a
# definition other objects see, a weak external the decorated one stands in
# for, and for a declaration with a guest exit thunk, the same, the
# decorated name itself a weak external the thunk stands in for, as llvm
# states them. a declaration with none names both undefined
fun function_label(e: *Emitter, f: id.Function) res[build_state.Label, *Error] {
    if (f::usize >= e.functions.len) { ret res[build_state.Label, *Error].err{stop(e, Error.symbol{module.Error.function{f}})}; }
    val held: opt[build_state.Label] = e.functions.data[f];
    if (sel held.some) { ret res[build_state.Label, *Error].ok{held.some}; }
    var data: res[FunctionData, module.Error] = module.function_data(e.m, f);
    if (sel data.err) { ret res[build_state.Label, *Error].err{stop(e, Error.symbol{data.err})}; }
    var spelled: vector.Vector[u8] = vector.init[u8](e.a);
    fin { vector.dnit[u8](?spelled); }
    val marked: res[bool, *Error] = decorated(e, ?data.ok, ?spelled);
    if (sel marked.err) { ret res[build_state.Label, *Error].err{marked.err}; }
    val spelling: View                           = View{data: spelled.data::*char, len: spelled.len};
    val l:        res[build_state.Label, *Error] = declared_label(e, marked.ok, spelling, data.ok.name);
    if (sel l.err) { ret l; }
    var size: build_state.Size = build_state.Size.none{};
    val unit: opt[u32]         = e.emitters.data[f];
    if (sel unit.some) { size = build_state.Size.measured{build_state.Difference{plus: e.ends.data[unit.some], minus: l.ok, addend: 0}}; }
    var shows: build_state.Exposure   = exposure(data.ok.linkage, ?symbol.FUNCTION, size);
    var guest: opt[build_state.Label] = opt[build_state.Label].none{};
    if (marked.ok && sel unit.none) {
        val g: res[opt[build_state.Label], *Error] = guest_of(e, spelling);
        if (sel g.err) { ret res[build_state.Label, *Error].err{g.err}; }
        guest = g.ok;
        if (sel guest.some) { shows.binding = ?symbol.WEAKLY; }
    }
    val shown: err[build_refusal.Refusal] = expose(e, l.ok, shows);
    if (sel shown.err) { ret res[build_state.Label, *Error].err{stop(e, Error.builder{shown.err})}; }
    e.functions.data[f] = opt[build_state.Label].some{l.ok};
    if (sel guest.some) {
        val fell: err[*Error] = builder(e, build_label.fall_back(e.b, l.ok, guest.some, ?symbol.ANTI_DEPENDENCY));
        if (sel fell.err) { ret res[build_state.Label, *Error].err{fell.err}; }
    }
    if (!marked.ok) { ret res[build_state.Label, *Error].ok{l.ok}; }
    if ((sel unit.some && symbol.binds(data.ok.linkage.binding, symbol.EXTERNAL)) || sel guest.some) {
        val p: res[build_state.Label, *Error] = anti_dependency(e, module.name_of(e.m, data.ok.name), l.ok);
        if (sel p.err) { ret p; }
        e.plain.data[f] = opt[build_state.Label].some{p.ok};
    }
    or (sel unit.none) {
        val p: res[build_state.Label, *Error] = handled(e, data.ok.name);
        if (sel p.err) { ret p; }
        val plain: err[build_refusal.Refusal] = expose(e, p.ok, exposure(data.ok.linkage, ?symbol.FUNCTION, build_state.Size.none{}));
        if (sel plain.err) { ret res[build_state.Label, *Error].err{stop(e, Error.builder{plain.err})}; }
        e.plain.data[f] = opt[build_state.Label].some{p.ok};
    }
    ret res[build_state.Label, *Error].ok{l.ok};
}

# the label an address of a function is taken through: the name the other
# convention's code reaches a declared function by where its native name is
# decorated, so the address is the one that code takes, and the function's
# own label otherwise
fun address_label(e: *Emitter, f: id.Function) res[build_state.Label, *Error] {
    val l: res[build_state.Label, *Error] = function_label(e, f);
    if (sel l.err) { ret l; }
    val plain: opt[build_state.Label] = e.plain.data[f];
    val unit:  opt[u32]               = e.emitters.data[f];
    if (sel plain.some) {
        if (sel unit.none) { ret res[build_state.Label, *Error].ok{plain.some}; }
    }
    ret l;
}

# the label of a function or global a reference of a relocation kind names: a
# function's own label for a branch to it, which the link may route through a
# stub, and the label its address is taken through for any other
fun reached_label(e: *Emitter, s: id.Symbol, kind: *reloc.Kind) res[build_state.Label, *Error] {
    if (sel s.function) {
        if (!reloc.has(kind, reloc.PLT)) { ret address_label(e, s.function); }
    }
    ret symbol_label(e, s);
}

# the label of a function or global an address in data names
fun datum_label(e: *Emitter, s: id.Symbol) res[build_state.Label, *Error] {
    if (sel s.function) { ret address_label(e, s.function); }
    ret symbol_label(e, s);
}

# the bridge one attribute of a thunk states, of a role. a guest exit
# thunk's row names the thunk first and the function it stands in for second,
# as llvm's arm64ec symbol map does, and every other names the function first
fun bridge_of(e: *Emitter, thunk: id.Function, at: *Attribute, role: *mink_bridge.Role) err[*Error] {
    val datum: Datum = at.datum;
    if (!(sel datum.text)) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.symbol{module.Error.function{thunk}})}; }
    val found: opt[id.Symbol] = module.find(e.m, datum.text);
    if (sel found.none) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.symbol{module.Error.function{thunk}})}; }
    val served: id.Symbol = found.some;
    if (!(sel served.function)) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.symbol{module.Error.function{thunk}})}; }
    val own: res[build_state.Label, *Error] = function_label(e, thunk);
    if (sel own.err) { ret err[*Error].err{own.err}; }
    var target: res[build_state.Label, *Error] = address_label(e, served.function);
    if (role == ?mink_bridge.ENTRY)      { target = function_label(e, served.function); }
    if (sel target.err)                  { ret err[*Error].err{target.err}; }
    if (role == ?mink_bridge.GUEST_EXIT) { ret builder(e, build_label.bridge(e.b, own.ok, target.ok, role)); }
    ret builder(e, build_label.bridge(e.b, target.ok, own.ok, role));
}

# each bridge a thunk of the module states it serves, as its register
# attributes name the function: an entry thunk to the function it enters, an
# exit thunk from the name the callee's emulated code is reached by, and a
# guest exit thunk to that name
fun bridges(e: *Emitter) err[*Error] {
    if (sel e.bridging.none) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < e.m.functions.len) {
        val thunk: id.Function = (i::u32);
        var k:     usize       = 0;
        for (k < e.m.functions.data[i].attributes.len) {
            val at: *Attribute = ?e.m.functions.data[i].attributes.data[k];
            k = k + 1;
            var role: opt[*mink_bridge.Role] = opt[*mink_bridge.Role].none{};
            if (schema.is(at, schema.ENTRY)) { role = opt[*mink_bridge.Role].some{?mink_bridge.ENTRY}; }
            or (schema.is(at, schema.EXIT))  { role = opt[*mink_bridge.Role].some{?mink_bridge.EXIT}; }
            or (schema.is(at, schema.GUEST)) { role = opt[*mink_bridge.Role].some{?mink_bridge.GUEST_EXIT}; }
            if (sel role.some) {
                val made: err[*Error] = bridge_of(e, thunk, at, role.some);
                if (sel made.err) { ret made; }
            }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# the label of a global of the module, a data symbol of the object made when it
# is first named, sized when the module defines it
fun global_label(e: *Emitter, g: id.Global) res[build_state.Label, *Error] {
    if (g::usize >= e.globals.len) { ret res[build_state.Label, *Error].err{stop(e, Error.symbol{module.Error.global{g}})}; }
    val held: opt[build_state.Label] = e.globals.data[g];
    if (sel held.some) { ret res[build_state.Label, *Error].ok{held.some}; }
    val data: res[GlobalData, module.Error] = module.global_data(e.m, g);
    if (sel data.err) { ret res[build_state.Label, *Error].err{stop(e, Error.symbol{data.err})}; }
    var size: build_state.Size = build_state.Size.none{};
    if (sel data.ok.initial.some) {
        val sized: res[u64, record.Error] = layout.size(?e.l, data.ok.type, DEFAULT_SPACE);
        if (sel sized.err) { ret res[build_state.Label, *Error].err{stop(e, Error.layout{Sized{global: g, error: sized.err}})}; }
        size = build_state.Size.fixed{sized.ok};
    }
    var kind: *symbol.Kind = ?symbol.DATA;
    if (sel data.ok.tls.some) { kind = ?symbol.TLS; }
    val l: res[build_state.Label, *Error] = handled(e, data.ok.name);
    if (sel l.err) { ret l; }
    val shown: err[build_refusal.Refusal] = expose(e, l.ok, exposure(data.ok.linkage, kind, size));
    if (sel shown.err) { ret res[build_state.Label, *Error].err{stop(e, Error.builder{shown.err})}; }
    e.globals.data[g] = opt[build_state.Label].some{l.ok};
    ret res[build_state.Label, *Error].ok{l.ok};
}

# the label of a function or global of the module
fun symbol_label(e: *Emitter, s: id.Symbol) res[build_state.Label, *Error] {
    if (sel s.function) { ret function_label(e, s.function); }
    ret global_label(e, s.global);
}

# the fixup kind a symbol or partner operand is applied as, with the instructions its relocation covers
fun fixup_of(b: *Body, at: Instruction, k: u32, own: mo.FixupKind, kind: *reloc.Kind) res[mo.FixupKind, *Error] {
    val found: fixup.Found = fixup.find(b.e.x, kind, own);
    if (sel found.bound)   { ret res[mo.FixupKind, *Error].ok{found.bound}; }
    if (sel found.unbound) { ret res[mo.FixupKind, *Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.unbound{site(b, at, k)})}; }
    ret res[mo.FixupKind, *Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.ambiguous{site(b, at, k)})};
}

# the fixup kind an operand position takes by default
fun own_fixup(o: *mo.Operand) mo.FixupKind {
    if (sel o.shape.immediate) { ret o.shape.immediate.fixup; }
    if (sel o.shape.relative)  { ret o.shape.relative.offset.fixup; }
    if (sel o.shape.memory)    { ret o.shape.memory.disp.fixup; }
    if (sel o.shape.marker)    { ret o.shape.marker; }
    ret mo.NO_FIXUP;
}

# the register a register operand is, none for anything allocation leaves
fun register_of(o: Operand) opt[Physical] {
    if (sel o.physical) { ret opt[Physical].some{o.physical}; }
    if (sel o.tied) {
        val dest: Register = o.tied.dest;
        if (sel dest.physical) { ret opt[Physical].some{dest.physical}; }
    }
    ret opt[Physical].none{};
}

# the instructions the relocation of a fixup kind covers, its own included
fun covered(e: *Emitter, fixup: mo.FixupKind) u32 {
    val s: opt[*core_fixup.Span] = core_fixup.span_of(e.opened.basis.set.spans, fixup);
    if (sel s.none) { ret 1; }
    ret s.some.count;
}

# why the registers an operand names cannot be given to masc's: a virtual
# one is unplaced and a cell no object holds
fun unplaced(b: *Body, at: Instruction, k: u32, o: Operand) opt[Error] {
    var names: [operand.MOST_NAMED]Register;
    val n:     u32 = operand.named(o, ?names[0]);
    var i:     u32 = 0;
    for (i < n) {
        val r: Register = names[i];
        if (sel r.virtual) { ret opt[Error].some{Error.unplaced{site(b, at, k)}}; }
        if (sel r.physical) {
            if (sel r.physical.cell) { ret opt[Error].some{Error.cell{site(b, at, k)}}; }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret opt[Error].none{};
}

# why a register an address names cannot be given to masc's, as `unplaced`
# finds it of the address's base, index and segment in turn
fun unplaced_at(b: *Body, at: Instruction, k: u32, r: opt[Register]) opt[Error] {
    if (sel r.none) { ret opt[Error].none{}; }
    val reg: Register = r.some;
    if (sel reg.virtual) { ret opt[Error].some{Error.unplaced{site(b, at, k)}}; }
    if (sel reg.physical) {
        if (sel reg.physical.cell) { ret opt[Error].some{Error.cell{site(b, at, k)}}; }
    }
    ret opt[Error].none{};
}

# a symbolic operand written into an instruction of a unit that requires constant time kept for the walk
fun note(b: *Body, n: Noted) err[*Error] {
    if (!b.timed) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    ret alloc(b.e, vector.push[Noted](?b.noted, n));
}

# whether an operand names a function or global or a partner's instruction, which a fixup is written for
fun symbolic(o: Operand) bool {
    if (sel o.symbol || sel o.partner) { ret true; }
    if (sel o.address) {
        val sym: opt[operand.Symbol] = o.address.symbol;
        ret sel sym.some;
    }
    ret false;
}

# whether a symbolic operand of a unit that requires constant time is among the instructions of `list` from `k` one
# sequence could cover
fun symbolic_ahead(b: *Body, list: Slice[Instruction], k: usize) bool {
    if (!b.timed) { ret false; }
    var j: usize = 0;
    for (j < relax.MAX_STEPS::usize && k + j < list.size) {
        val d: *InstructionData = function.data(b.u.code, list.data[k + j]);
        if (sel d.opcode.row) {
            var o: usize = 0;
            for (o < d.operands.size) {
                if (symbolic(d.operands.data[o])) { ret true; }
                o = o + 1;
            }
        }
        j = j + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# the symbolic operands noted while the `n` instructions of `list` from `k` were written at label `l`, each at the
# step of the sequence its instruction is
fun fixed(b: *Body, list: Slice[Instruction], k: usize, n: usize, l: opt[build_state.Label]) err[*Error] {
    fin { vector.truncate[Noted](?b.noted, 0); }
    if (sel l.none) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < b.noted.len) {
        val x: *Noted = ?b.noted.data[i];
        var j: usize  = 0;
        for (j < n && list.data[k + j] != x.at) { j = j + 1; }
        if (j < n) {
            val f:      Fixing      = Fixing{function: b.u.function, label: l.some, step: j::u32, operand: x.operand, fixup: x.fixup, symbol: x.symbol, addend: x.addend, partner: x.partner};
            val pushed: err[*Error] = alloc(b.e, vector.push[Fixing](?b.e.fixing, f));
            if (sel pushed.err) { ret pushed; }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# whether instruction `d` states what its memory accesses read, and so for a unit that requires constant time each is
# kept for the walk
fun states(b: *Body, d: *InstructionData) bool {
    if (!b.timed)            { ret false; }
    if (!(sel d.opcode.row)) { ret false; }
    ret d.metadata.secret || d.metadata.flags.public || metadata.states_extent(?d.metadata);
}

# whether a stated memory access is among the instructions of `list` from `k` one sequence could cover
fun stated_ahead(b: *Body, list: Slice[Instruction], k: usize) bool {
    var j: usize = 0;
    for (j < relax.MAX_STEPS::usize && k + j < list.size) {
        if (states(b, function.data(b.u.code, list.data[k + j]))) { ret true; }
        j = j + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# whether the effect `e` states an access through operand `k`
fun through(e: *effect.Effect, k: u32) bool {
    if (e == nil) { ret false; }
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < e.memory.len) {
        if (e.memory.at[i].operand::u32 == k) { ret true; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# each memory access instruction `at` makes written in row `r`, kept for the walk with the secrecy its metadata states,
# secret with its secret mark, public with the public flag, and the frame extent it states. an access is named as the
# walk names it: by the operand the row's effect states it through, by its position in the effect for one no operand
# names, then by each memory operand the effect states none of
fun state(b: *Body, at: Instruction, r: *rows.Row) err[*Error] {
    val d: *InstructionData = function.data(b.u.code, at);
    if (!states(b, d)) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    val secret:  bool            = d.metadata.secret;
    val secrecy: bool            = d.metadata.secret || d.metadata.flags.public;
    val framed:  metadata.Extent = d.metadata.extent;
    val e:       *effect.Effect  = r.effect;
    if (e != nil) {
        var i: u32 = 0;
        for (i < e.memory.len) {
            var named: walk.Accessor = walk.Accessor.index{i};
            val o:     u8            = e.memory.at[i].operand;
            if (o != field.NO_OPERAND) { named = walk.Accessor.operand{o}; }
            val kept: err[*Error] = alloc(b.e, vector.push[Stated](?b.stated, Stated{at: at, access: named, secrecy: secrecy, secret: secret, extent: framed}));
            if (sel kept.err) { ret kept; }
            i = i + 1;
        }
    }
    var k: u32 = 0;
    for (k < r.operands.len) {
        if (sel r.operands.at[k].shape.memory && !through(e, k)) {
            val kept: err[*Error] = alloc(b.e, vector.push[Stated](?b.stated, Stated{at: at, access: walk.Accessor.operand{k::u8}, secrecy: secrecy, secret: secret, extent: framed}));
            if (sel kept.err) { ret kept; }
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# the stated memory accesses kept while the `n` instructions of `list` from `k` were written at label `l`, each at the
# step of the sequence its instruction is
fun accessed(b: *Body, list: Slice[Instruction], k: usize, n: usize, l: opt[build_state.Label]) err[*Error] {
    fin { vector.truncate[Stated](?b.stated, 0); }
    if (sel l.none) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < b.stated.len) {
        val x: *Stated = ?b.stated.data[i];
        var j: usize   = 0;
        for (j < n && list.data[k + j] != x.at) { j = j + 1; }
        if (j < n) {
            val s:      Stating     = Stating{function: b.u.function, label: l.some, step: j::u32, access: x.access, secrecy: x.secrecy, secret: x.secret, extent: x.extent};
            val pushed: err[*Error] = alloc(b.e, vector.push[Stating](?b.e.stating, s));
            if (sel pushed.err) { ret pushed; }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# register `at` of the instruction `i` kept for the walk as one it leaves a declared secret in, but a location no
# register holds or a register that reads zero
fun declare(b: *Body, i: Instruction, at: Physical) err[*Error] {
    if (!(sel at.register)) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    val file: *rf.File          = b.e.opened.basis.set.codec.registers;
    val row:  opt[*rf.Register] = rf.row_of(file, at.register);
    if (sel row.none)                    { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    if ((row.some.flags & rf.ZERO) != 0) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    ret alloc(b.e, vector.push[Declared](?b.seeded, Declared{at: i, register: at.register}));
}

# each member of list `given` at row operand `ro` kept as `declare` keeps a register
fun declare_list(b: *Body, at: Instruction, file: *rf.File, ro: *mo.Operand, given: operand.List) err[*Error] {
    if (!(sel ro.shape.list)) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    var room: [instruction.MOST_MEMBERS]mo.Value;
    val v:    mo.Value = instruction.list_value(file, ?ro.shape.list, given, ?room[0]);
    if (!(sel v.list)) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    var m: u32 = 0;
    for (m < v.list.len) {
        val named: mo.Value = v.list.at[m];
        if (sel named.register) {
            val kept: err[*Error] = declare(b, at, Physical.register{named.register});
            if (sel kept.err) { ret kept; }
        }
        m = m + 1;
    }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# what instruction `at` written in row `r` leaves a declared secret in, kept for the walk where its metadata marks it
# secret: a call's results, the registers it writes beyond its operands, and any other instruction's written operands.
# a call also writes its link and what the convention clobbers, which hold no result, and selection marks secret no
# instruction of an expansion that writes a public register. an instruction that reads memory seeds nothing, as the
# walk takes what it reads from the bytes it places or from the access's statement, byte by byte, where the ir marks
# an aggregate secret whole
fun seed_results(b: *Body, at: Instruction, r: *rows.Row) err[*Error] {
    if (!b.timed) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    val d:    *InstructionData = function.data(b.u.code, at);
    val file: *rf.File         = b.e.opened.basis.set.codec.registers;
    if (!d.metadata.secret || !(sel d.opcode.row) || file == nil) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    if (reads_memory(b, d, r))                                    { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    val got: query.Answer[effect.Control] = instruction.transfer(file, d);
    if (sel got.decided && got.decided.transfer == effect.CALL) {
        var i: usize = 0;
        for (i < d.implicit.size) {
            if (d.implicit.data[i].write) {
                val kept: err[*Error] = declare(b, at, d.implicit.data[i].location);
                if (sel kept.err) { ret kept; }
            }
            i = i + 1;
        }
        ret err[*Error].ok{};
    }
    var k: u32 = 0;
    for (k::usize < d.operands.size) {
        val o: Operand = d.operands.data[k];
        if ((instruction.stated_role(b.e.opened.basis.set, d, k) & mo.WRITE) != 0) {
            val reg: opt[Physical] = register_of(o);
            if (sel reg.some) {
                val kept: err[*Error] = declare(b, at, reg.some);
                if (sel kept.err) { ret kept; }
            }
            if (sel o.list) {
                val kept: err[*Error] = declare_list(b, at, file, ?r.operands.at[k], o.list);
                if (sel kept.err) { ret kept; }
            }
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# whether `d`, written in row `r`, reads memory: through a memory operand, or by an access its row's effect states,
# as a load through a register operand
fun reads_memory(b: *Body, d: *InstructionData, r: *rows.Row) bool {
    var k: u32 = 0;
    for (k::usize < d.operands.size) {
        val o: Operand = d.operands.data[k];
        if ((sel o.address || sel o.slot) && (instruction.stated_role(b.e.opened.basis.set, d, k) & mo.READ) != 0) { ret true; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    if (r.effect == nil) { ret false; }
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < r.effect.memory.len) {
        val acc:  *effect.Access = ?r.effect.memory.at[i];
        var role: mo.Role        = acc.role;
        if (role == mo.NONE && acc.operand::u32 < r.operands.len) { role = r.operands.at[acc.operand].role; }
        if ((role & mo.READ) != 0)                                { ret true; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# whether instruction `d` is of the function's own timing switch: an instruction of a row a step of the switch encodes,
# which only selection's placing of the switch writes, an inline block being one instruction of its own opcode
fun switching(b: *Body, d: *InstructionData) bool {
    if (!(sel d.opcode.row)) { ret false; }
    if (sel b.switch.none)   { ret false; }
    val sw:    *mswitch.Switch  = b.switch.some.switch;
    val set:   *masc_set.Set    = b.e.opened.basis.set;
    val lists: [3]mswitch.Steps = [3]mswitch.Steps{sw.read, sw.set, sw.restore};
    var l:     usize            = 0;
    for (l < 3) {
        val steps: mswitch.Steps = lists[l];
        l = l + 1;
        var n: u32 = 0;
        for (n < steps.len) {
            if (rows.at(set.codec.rows, steps.at[n].row) == d.opcode.row) { ret true; }
            n = n + 1;
        }
    }
    ret false;
}

# whether instruction `d` is an inline block one of whose operands' memory holds a pointer whose type states what it
# reaches
fun pointing(d: *InstructionData) bool {
    if (!(sel d.opcode.inline)) { ret false; }
    ret (d.opcode.inline.publics | d.opcode.inline.secrets) != 0;
}

# whether an instruction the walk takes a fact of is among the instructions of `list` from `k` one sequence could cover
fun marked_ahead(b: *Body, list: Slice[Instruction], k: usize) bool {
    var j: usize = 0;
    for (j < relax.MAX_STEPS::usize && k + j < list.size) {
        val d: *InstructionData = function.data(b.u.code, list.data[k + j]);
        if (switching(b, d) || sel d.opcode.inline) { ret true; }
        j = j + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# the facts the walk takes of the `n` instructions of `list` from `k` written at label `l`, each at the step of the
# sequence its instruction is: each of the timing switch, each instruction of an inline block, as the block's encode
# counted them in `b.steps`, and each of those naming an operand whose memory holds a pointer its type states what it
# reaches of, as the encode counted it in `b.uses`
fun marked(b: *Body, list: Slice[Instruction], k: usize, n: usize, l: opt[build_state.Label]) err[*Error] {
    fin { vector.truncate[masc_inline.Use](?b.uses, 0); }
    if (sel l.none) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    var j: usize = 0;
    for (j < n) {
        val d: *InstructionData = function.data(b.u.code, list.data[k + j]);
        if (switching(b, d)) {
            val pushed: err[*Error] = alloc(b.e, vector.push[Marking](?b.e.marking, Marking{function: b.u.function, label: l.some, step: j::u32, fact: timed.Fact.switch{}}));
            if (sel pushed.err) { ret pushed; }
        }
        val op: Opcode = d.opcode;
        if (sel op.inline) {
            val x: *Inline = op.inline;
            var s: u32     = 0;
            for (s < b.steps) {
                val res_inlined: err[*Error] = alloc(b.e, vector.push[Marking](?b.e.marking, Marking{function: b.u.function, label: l.some, step: j::u32 + s, fact: timed.Fact.inline{}}));
                if (sel res_inlined.err) { ret res_inlined; }
                s = s + 1;
            }
            var i: usize = 0;
            for (i < b.uses.len) {
                val u:   masc_inline.Use = b.uses.data[i];
                val bit: u32             = 1::u32 << u.operand;
                i = i + 1;
                if (u.operand >= 32 || ((x.publics | x.secrets) & bit) == 0) { cnt; }
                val fact:   timed.Fact  = timed.Fact.pointer{(x.secrets & bit) != 0};
                val pushed: err[*Error] = alloc(b.e, vector.push[Marking](?b.e.marking, Marking{function: b.u.function, label: l.some, step: j::u32 + u.step, fact: fact}));
                if (sel pushed.err) { ret pushed; }
            }
        }
        j = j + 1;
    }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# the registers kept while the `n` instructions of `list` from `k` were written at label `l`, each at the step of the
# sequence its instruction is, but those of a call that trusts its callee, whose model states its results as the
# callee's declaration does (`contract.results`)
fun seeded(b: *Body, list: Slice[Instruction], k: usize, n: usize, l: opt[build_state.Label]) err[*Error] {
    fin { vector.truncate[Declared](?b.seeded, 0); }
    if (sel l.none) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    val trusting: opt[Instruction] = trusting_call(b, list, k, n);
    var i:        usize            = 0;
    for (i < b.seeded.len) {
        val x: *Declared = ?b.seeded.data[i];
        i = i + 1;
        if (sel trusting.some) {
            if (x.at == trusting.some) { cnt; }
        }
        var j: usize = 0;
        for (j < n && list.data[k + j] != x.at) { j = j + 1; }
        if (j < n) {
            val s:      Seeding     = Seeding{function: b.u.function, label: l.some, step: j::u32, register: x.register};
            val pushed: err[*Error] = alloc(b.e, vector.push[Seeding](?b.e.seeding, s));
            if (sel pushed.err) { ret pushed; }
        }
    }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# the call among the `n` instructions of `list` from `k` that trusts its callee (`contract.trusted`), as the call site
# just kept of them names it, none for none
fun trusting_call(b: *Body, list: Slice[Instruction], k: usize, n: usize) opt[Instruction] {
    if (b.e.calling.len == 0) { ret opt[Instruction].none{}; }
    val c: *Calling = ?b.e.calling.data[b.e.calling.len - 1];
    if (sel c.callee.none) { ret opt[Instruction].none{}; }
    var j: usize = 0;
    for (j < n) {
        if (list.data[k + j] == c.instruction) {
            if (contract.trusted(b.e.m, b.u.function, c.callee.some)) { ret opt[Instruction].some{c.instruction}; }
            ret opt[Instruction].none{};
        }
        j = j + 1;
    }
    ret opt[Instruction].none{};
}

# `v` as the next operand of `ins`, which masc reads when the instruction is written
fun hand(ins: *masc_emit.Instruction, v: mo.Value) {
    ins.step.values[ins.given] = v;
    ins.given                  = ins.given + 1;
}

# an address given to masc's at a memory position, its symbol bound to its
# label and fixup kind, answering how many instructions its relocation covers
fun give_address(b: *Body, at: Instruction, ins: *masc_emit.Instruction, k: u32, ro: *mo.Operand, a: operand.Address) res[u32, *Error] {
    if (!(sel ro.shape.memory)) { ret res[u32, *Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.shape{site(b, at, k)})}; }
    val v: mo.Value = instruction.address_value(a);
    if (!(sel v.memory)) { ret res[u32, *Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.unplaced{site(b, at, k)})}; }
    var made: mo.Address          = v.memory;
    var span: u32                 = 1;
    val sym:  opt[operand.Symbol] = a.symbol;
    if (sel sym.some) {
        val l: res[build_state.Label, *Error] = reached_label(b.e, sym.some.symbol, sym.some.kind);
        if (sel l.err) { ret res[u32, *Error].err{l.err}; }
        val f: res[mo.FixupKind, *Error] = fixup_of(b, at, k, own_fixup(ro), sym.some.kind);
        if (sel f.err) { ret res[u32, *Error].err{f.err}; }
        made.symbol = mo.Symbol{id: l.ok, addend: sym.some.addend, fixup: f.ok};
        span        = covered(b.e, f.ok);
        val kept: err[*Error] = note(b, Noted{at: at, operand: k::u8, fixup: f.ok, symbol: opt[id.Symbol].some{sym.some.symbol}, addend: sym.some.addend, partner: opt[build_state.Label].none{}});
        if (sel kept.err) { ret res[u32, *Error].err{kept.err}; }
    }
    hand(ins, mo.Value.memory{made});
    ret res[u32, *Error].ok{span};
}

# operand `k` of an instruction given to masc's, answering how many
# instructions its relocation covers. a list's members are written to
# `room`, which holds instruction.MOST_MEMBERS and outlives the instruction's
# writing, from `used` on
fun give(b: *Body, at: Instruction, ins: *masc_emit.Instruction, k: u32, o: Operand, room: *mo.Value, used: *u32) res[u32, *Error] {
    val e:  *Emitter    = b.e;
    val ro: *mo.Operand = ?ins.step.row.operands.at[k];
    if (sel o.address) {
        val base: opt[Error] = unplaced_at(b, at, k, o.address.base);
        if (sel base.some) { ret res[u32, *Error].err{stop(b.e, base.some)}; }
        val index: opt[Error] = unplaced_at(b, at, k, o.address.index);
        if (sel index.some) { ret res[u32, *Error].err{stop(b.e, index.some)}; }
        val segment: opt[Error] = unplaced_at(b, at, k, o.address.segment);
        if (sel segment.some) { ret res[u32, *Error].err{stop(b.e, segment.some)}; }
        ret give_address(b, at, ins, k, ro, o.address);
    }
    if (sel o.list) {
        val why: opt[Error] = unplaced(b, at, k, o);
        if (sel why.some) { ret res[u32, *Error].err{stop(b.e, why.some)}; }
    }
    if (sel o.list) {
        if (!(sel ro.shape.list))                                 { ret res[u32, *Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.shape{site(b, at, k)})}; }
        if (@used + o.list.count::u32 > instruction.MOST_MEMBERS) { ret res[u32, *Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.shape{site(b, at, k)})}; }
        val v: mo.Value = instruction.list_value(function.file(b.u.code), ?ro.shape.list, o.list, ?room[@used]);
        if (!(sel v.list)) { ret res[u32, *Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.shape{site(b, at, k)})}; }
        @used = @used + o.list.count::u32;
        hand(ins, mo.Value.list{v.list});
        ret res[u32, *Error].ok{1};
    }
    if (sel o.literal) {
        if (!(sel ro.shape.literal)) { ret res[u32, *Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.shape{site(b, at, k)})}; }
        hand(ins, mo.Value.literal{o.literal});
        ret res[u32, *Error].ok{1};
    }
    if (sel o.virtual || sel o.slot)           { ret res[u32, *Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.unplaced{site(b, at, k)})}; }
    if (sel o.tied && sel o.tied.dest.virtual) { ret res[u32, *Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.unplaced{site(b, at, k)})}; }
    if (sel o.physical && sel o.physical.cell) { ret res[u32, *Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.cell{site(b, at, k)})}; }
    if (sel o.physical && sel ro.shape.id) {
        val v: mo.Value = instruction.value_of(ro, o);
        if (!(sel v.id)) { ret res[u32, *Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.shape{site(b, at, k)})}; }
        hand(ins, mo.Value.id{v.id});
        ret res[u32, *Error].ok{1};
    }
    val reg: opt[Physical] = register_of(o);
    if (sel reg.some) {
        val place: Physical = reg.some;
        if (!(sel ro.shape.register)) { ret res[u32, *Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.shape{site(b, at, k)})}; }
        if (!(sel place.register))    { ret res[u32, *Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.shape{site(b, at, k)})}; }
        hand(ins, mo.Value.register{place.register});
        ret res[u32, *Error].ok{1};
    }
    if (sel o.immediate) {
        val v: mo.Value = instruction.value_of(ro, o);
        if (!(sel v.immediate || sel v.enumerant || sel v.condition)) { ret res[u32, *Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.shape{site(b, at, k)})}; }
        hand(ins, v);
        ret res[u32, *Error].ok{1};
    }
    if (sel o.block) {
        if (!(sel ro.shape.relative)) { ret res[u32, *Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.shape{site(b, at, k)})}; }
        hand(ins, mo.Value.symbol{mo.Symbol{id: b.blocks.data[o.block], addend: 0, fixup: mo.NO_FIXUP}});
        ret res[u32, *Error].ok{1};
    }
    if (sel o.symbol) {
        if (!(sel ro.shape.immediate || sel ro.shape.relative || sel ro.shape.marker)) { ret res[u32, *Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.shape{site(b, at, k)})}; }
        val l: res[build_state.Label, *Error] = reached_label(e, o.symbol.symbol, o.symbol.kind);
        if (sel l.err) { ret res[u32, *Error].err{l.err}; }
        val f: res[mo.FixupKind, *Error] = fixup_of(b, at, k, own_fixup(ro), o.symbol.kind);
        if (sel f.err) { ret res[u32, *Error].err{f.err}; }
        hand(ins, mo.Value.symbol{mo.Symbol{id: l.ok, addend: o.symbol.addend, fixup: f.ok}});
        val kept: err[*Error] = note(b, Noted{at: at, operand: k::u8, fixup: f.ok, symbol: opt[id.Symbol].some{o.symbol.symbol}, addend: o.symbol.addend, partner: opt[build_state.Label].none{}});
        if (sel kept.err) { ret res[u32, *Error].err{kept.err}; }
        ret res[u32, *Error].ok{covered(e, f.ok)};
    }
    if (sel o.partner) {
        if (!(sel ro.shape.immediate || sel ro.shape.relative)) { ret res[u32, *Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.shape{site(b, at, k)})}; }
        val mark: opt[*build_state.Label] = map.get[u32, build_state.Label](?b.marks, ?o.partner.label);
        if (sel mark.none) { ret res[u32, *Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.label{site(b, at, k)})}; }
        val f: res[mo.FixupKind, *Error] = fixup_of(b, at, k, own_fixup(ro), o.partner.kind);
        if (sel f.err) { ret res[u32, *Error].err{f.err}; }
        hand(ins, mo.Value.symbol{mo.Symbol{id: (@mark.some), addend: 0, fixup: f.ok}});
        val kept: err[*Error] = note(b, Noted{at: at, operand: k::u8, fixup: f.ok, symbol: opt[id.Symbol].none{}, addend: 0, partner: opt[build_state.Label].some{@mark.some}});
        if (sel kept.err) { ret res[u32, *Error].err{kept.err}; }
        ret res[u32, *Error].ok{covered(e, f.ok)};
    }
    ret res[u32, *Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.shape{site(b, at, k)})};
}

# an instruction given to masc's, answering how many instructions the
# relocations of its operands cover, the members of its lists written to
# `room`, which holds instruction.MOST_MEMBERS
fun start(b: *Body, at: Instruction, ins: *masc_emit.Instruction, room: *mo.Value) res[u32, *Error] {
    val d:  *InstructionData = function.data(b.u.code, at);
    val op: Opcode           = d.opcode;
    if (!(sel op.row)) { ret res[u32, *Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.pseudo{site(b, at, NO_OPERAND)})}; }
    val row: *rows.Row = written(b, d, op.row);
    if (d.operands.size != row.operands.len::usize) { ret res[u32, *Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.shape{site(b, at, NO_OPERAND)})}; }
    ins.step.row    = row;
    ins.step.marker = mo.NO_FIXUP;
    ins.step.form   = core_form.PREFERRED;
    ins.given       = 0;
    var span: u32 = 1;
    var used: u32 = 0;
    var k:    u32 = 0;
    for (k::usize < d.operands.size) {
        val given: res[u32, *Error] = give(b, at, ins, k, d.operands.data[k], room, ?used);
        if (sel given.err)   { ret given; }
        if (given.ok > span) { span = given.ok; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    val kept: err[*Error] = state(b, at, ins.step.row);
    if (sel kept.err) { ret res[u32, *Error].err{kept.err}; }
    val declared: err[*Error] = seed_results(b, at, ins.step.row);
    if (sel declared.err) { ret res[u32, *Error].err{declared.err}; }
    ret res[u32, *Error].ok{span};
}

# the row instruction `d` of row `r` is handed to masc in: the first short form
# of `r` whose fixed registers its operands hold and whose requirement the
# view admits, else `r`
fun written(b: *Body, d: *InstructionData, r: *rows.Row) *rows.Row {
    val s: Shorts = b.e.shorts;
    var i: u32    = 0;
    for (i < s.len) {
        val c: *Short = ?s.at[i];
        i = i + 1;
        if (c.long != r)                                                                    { cnt; }
        if (holds(b, d, c.short) && core_state.admits(trait.view(b.e.b), c.short.requires)) { ret c.short; }
    }
    ret r;
}

# whether the operands of instruction `d` hold, at each operand row `r` fixes, the register it fixes there
fun holds(b: *Body, d: *InstructionData, r: *rows.Row) bool {
    if (d.operands.size != r.operands.len::usize) { ret false; }
    var k: u32 = 0;
    for (k < r.operands.len) {
        val f: opt[rf.Id] = codec.fixed(b.e.opened.basis.set.codec, r, k::u8);
        if (sel f.some) {
            val reg: opt[Physical] = register_of(d.operands.data[k]);
            if (sel reg.none)                { ret false; }
            if (!(sel reg.some.register))    { ret false; }
            if (reg.some.register != f.some) { ret false; }
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret true;
}

# the location masc reads of operand `k` of an inline block: the register it
# names, the address it holds or the constant it is
fun location_of(b: *Body, at: Instruction, k: u32, o: Operand) res[masc_inline.Location, *Error] {
    val why: opt[Error] = unplaced(b, at, k, o);
    if (sel why.some) { ret res[masc_inline.Location, *Error].err{stop(b.e, why.some)}; }
    if (sel o.address) {
        val v: mo.Value = instruction.address_value(o.address);
        if (!(sel v.memory)) { ret res[masc_inline.Location, *Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.unplaced{site(b, at, k)})}; }
        ret res[masc_inline.Location, *Error].ok{v};
    }
    if (sel o.immediate)                       { ret res[masc_inline.Location, *Error].ok{mo.Value.immediate{o.immediate}}; }
    if (sel o.virtual || sel o.slot)           { ret res[masc_inline.Location, *Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.unplaced{site(b, at, k)})}; }
    if (sel o.tied && sel o.tied.dest.virtual) { ret res[masc_inline.Location, *Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.unplaced{site(b, at, k)})}; }
    val reg: opt[Physical] = register_of(o);
    if (sel reg.some) {
        val place: Physical = reg.some;
        if (sel place.register) { ret res[masc_inline.Location, *Error].ok{mo.Value.register{place.register}}; }
        ret res[masc_inline.Location, *Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.cell{site(b, at, k)})};
    }
    ret res[masc_inline.Location, *Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.shape{site(b, at, k)})};
}

# an inline block handed to masc with each operand at its location, which masc encodes at the cursor
fun encode_inline(b: *Body, at: Instruction, x: *Inline) err[*Error] {
    val d:    *InstructionData = function.data(b.u.code, at);
    var held: [ia.MOST_OPERANDS]masc_inline.Location;
    if (d.operands.size > ia.MOST_OPERANDS::usize) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.shape{site(b, at, NO_OPERAND)})}; }
    var k: u32 = 0;
    for (k::usize < d.operands.size) {
        val got: res[masc_inline.Location, *Error] = location_of(b, at, k, d.operands.data[k]);
        if (sel got.err) { ret err[*Error].err{got.err}; }
        held[k] = got.ok;
        k       = k + 1;
    }
    val before:  usize       = build_label.label_count(b.e.b);
    val entered: err[*Error] = builder(b.e, build_emit.under(b.e.b, x.context));
    if (sel entered.err) { ret entered; }
    var uses:  *vector.Vector[masc_inline.Use] = nil;
    var steps: *u32                            = nil;
    if (b.timed && pointing(d)) { uses = ?b.uses; }
    if (b.timed)                { steps = ?b.steps; }
    val encoded: err[build_refusal.Refusal] = masc_inline.encode(?x.block, masc_inline.Locations{at: ?held[0], len: d.operands.size::u32}, b.e.b, uses, steps);
    if (sel encoded.err)                             { ret err[*Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.inline{Encoded{at: site(b, at, NO_OPERAND), message: encoded.err.message}})}; }
    if (b.timed && b.steps == masc_inline.UNCOUNTED) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.inline{Encoded{at: site(b, at, NO_OPERAND), message: UNCOUNTED}})}; }
    val left: err[*Error] = builder(b.e, build_emit.under(b.e.b, b.u.context));
    if (sel left.err) { ret left; }
    var n: usize = before + 1;
    for (n <= build_label.label_count(b.e.b)) {
        val l:    build_state.Label = (n::u32);
        val name: opt[View]         = build.label_name(b.e.b, l);
        if (sel name.some) {
            val kept: err[*Error] = alloc(b.e, vector.push[build_state.Label](?b.e.named, l));
            if (sel kept.err) { ret kept; }
        }
        n = n + 1;
    }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# the linkage of a symbol an inline block names and the module does not have, as an ir declaration's default
val DECLARED: Linkage = Linkage{binding: ?symbol.GLOBAL, visibility: ?symbol.DEFAULT};

# each name inline blocks reference that nothing placed or exposed made a
# symbol of the object: the module's function or global of that name, else
# an undefined symbol
fun declare_named(e: *Emitter) err[*Error] {
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < e.named.len) {
        val l:     build_state.Label         = e.named.data[i];
        val shown: opt[build_state.Exposure] = build.exposure_of(e.b, l);
        val name:  opt[View]                 = build.label_name(e.b, l);
        i = i + 1;
        if (build_label.bound(e.b, l) || sel shown.some) { cnt; }
        if (sel name.none)                               { cnt; }
        val own: opt[id.Symbol] = module.find(e.m, name.some);
        if (sel own.some) {
            val made: res[build_state.Label, *Error] = symbol_label(e, own.some);
            if (sel made.err) { ret err[*Error].err{made.err}; }
            cnt;
        }
        # the text does not state what the symbol is, so it has no kind
        val exposed: err[*Error] = builder(e, build_label.expose(e.b, l, exposure(DECLARED, ?symbol.NOTYPE, build_state.Size.none{})));
        if (sel exposed.err) { ret exposed; }
    }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# the list members the instructions of one sequence keep room for
val ROOM: u32 = relax.MAX_STEPS * instruction.MOST_MEMBERS;

# the instructions of a block from position `k`, one instruction or the sequence its relocation covers
# ---
# ret: how many instructions were written
fun write(b: *Body, list: Slice[Instruction], k: usize) res[usize, *Error] {
    val at: Instruction = list.data[k];
    val op: Opcode      = function.data(b.u.code, at).opcode;
    if (sel op.inline) {
        val done: err[*Error] = encode_inline(b, at, op.inline);
        if (sel done.err) { ret res[usize, *Error].err{done.err}; }
        ret res[usize, *Error].ok{1};
    }
    val steps:  *masc_emit.Instruction = ?b.e.steps[0];
    val listed: *mo.Value              = ?b.e.listed[0];
    val span:   res[u32, *Error]       = start(b, at, steps, listed);
    if (sel span.err) { ret res[usize, *Error].err{span.err}; }
    if (span.ok <= 1) {
        val put: err[*Error] = builder(b.e, lone(b, steps));
        if (sel put.err) { ret res[usize, *Error].err{put.err}; }
        ret res[usize, *Error].ok{1};
    }
    if (span.ok > relax.MAX_STEPS || k + span.ok::usize > list.size) { ret res[usize, *Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.span{site(b, at, NO_OPERAND)})}; }
    var j: u32 = 1;
    for (j < span.ok) {
        val next: Instruction = list.data[k + j::usize];
        if (function.data(b.u.code, next).label != instruction.NO_LABEL) { ret res[usize, *Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.label{site(b, next, NO_OPERAND)})}; }
        val covers: res[u32, *Error] = start(b, next, ?steps[j], ?listed[j * instruction.MOST_MEMBERS]);
        if (sel covers.err) { ret res[usize, *Error].err{covers.err}; }
        j = j + 1;
    }
    val put: err[*Error] = builder(b.e, masc_emit.sequence(b.e.b, ?steps[0], span.ok));
    if (sel put.err) { ret res[usize, *Error].err{put.err}; }
    ret res[usize, *Error].ok{span.ok::usize};
}

# one instruction written alone: read against its row under a checked build, and otherwise taken as selection made it
fun lone(b: *Body, ins: *masc_emit.Instruction) err[build_refusal.Refusal] {
    if (b.u.code.checked) { ret masc_emit.put(b.e.b, ins); }
    var one: inst.Inst = inst.Inst{row: ins.step.row, values: ?ins.step.values[0], count: ins.given, form: ins.step.form};
    ret build_emit.emit_trusted(b.e.b, ?one, mo.NO_FIXUP);
}

# the labels of a function's blocks and of the instructions its partner operands name
fun label_body(b: *Body) err[*Error] {
    val code: *Function = b.u.code;
    var i:    usize     = 0;
    for (i < code.blocks.len) {
        val l: res[build_state.Label, build_refusal.Refusal] = build_label.anonymous(b.e.b);
        if (sel l.err) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.builder{l.err})}; }
        val pushed: err[*Error] = alloc(b.e, vector.push[build_state.Label](?b.blocks, l.ok));
        if (sel pushed.err) { ret pushed; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < b.u.laid.order.len) {
        val list: Slice[Instruction] = function.instructions(code, b.u.laid.order.data[i]);
        var k:    usize              = 0;
        for (k < list.size) {
            val n: u32 = function.data(code, list.data[k]).label;
            if (n != instruction.NO_LABEL) {
                if (map.contains[u32, build_state.Label](?b.marks, ?n)) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.label{site(b, list.data[k], NO_OPERAND)})}; }
                val l: res[build_state.Label, build_refusal.Refusal] = build_label.anonymous(b.e.b);
                if (sel l.err) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.builder{l.err})}; }
                val stored: res[bool, allocator.Error] = map.insert[u32, build_state.Label](?b.marks, n, l.ok);
                if (sel stored.err) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.alloc{stored.err})}; }
            }
            k = k + 1;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# a call frame fact handed to masc: a rule, or an epilogue scope's begin or end
fun hand_fact(b: *Body, stated: Statement) err[*Error] {
    if (sel stated.rule)  { ret builder(b.e, frame.cfi(b.e.b, stated.rule)); }
    if (sel stated.begin) { ret builder(b.e, frame.cfi_epilogue_begin(b.e.b)); }
    ret builder(b.e, frame.cfi_epilogue_end(b.e.b));
}

# the call frame facts at an instruction handed to masc, those that come
# before it or those that follow it
fun hand_facts(b: *Body, at: Instruction, after: bool) err[*Error] {
    if (!b.e.framed)              { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    if (at::usize >= b.facts.len) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    var f: u32 = b.facts.data[at];
    for (f != NONE) {
        val fact: *Fact = ?b.u.facts.data[f];
        if (fact.after == after) {
            val handed: err[*Error] = hand_fact(b, fact.stated);
            if (sel handed.err) { ret handed; }
            b.given.data[f] = true;
        }
        f = b.next.data[f];
    }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# the label before an instruction a range begins or ends at placed
fun mark_range(b: *Body, at: Instruction) err[*Error] {
    val held: opt[*Mark] = map.get[u32, Mark](?b.ranged, ?at);
    if (sel held.none)     { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    if (held.some.defined) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    held.some.defined = true;
    ret builder(b.e, build_label.define(b.e.b, held.some.label));
}

# the source location of an instruction stated when it changes, an
# instruction with none stated as line 0 of the last file
fun state_line(b: *Body, at: Instruction) err[*Error] {
    if (!b.e.stated) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    val loc: opt[debug_record.Location] = function.data(b.u.code, at).metadata.location;
    if (b.spoke) {
        if (sel loc.none && sel b.at.none) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
        if (sel loc.some) {
            val was: opt[debug_record.Location] = b.at;
            if (sel was.some) {
                if (was.some == loc.some) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
            }
        }
    }
    b.spoke = true;
    b.at    = loc;
    var row: masc_line.Location = masc_line.Location{file: 0, line: 0, column: 0, end_column: opt[u32].none{}, flags: 0, isa: 0, discriminator: 0};
    if (sel loc.some) {
        val p: res[debug_record.Position, debug_table.Error] = debug_place.position(?b.e.m.debug, loc.some);
        if (sel p.ok) {
            row.file   = p.ok.file;
            row.line   = p.ok.line;
            row.column = p.ok.column;
            row.flags  = mink_line.STATEMENT;
        }
    }
    val stated: err[*Error] = builder(b.e, masc_line.location(?b.e.lines, b.e.b, row));
    if (sel stated.err) { ret stated; }
    ret alloc(b.e, vector.push[Sourced](?b.e.sourced, Sourced{function: b.u.function, location: loc}));
}

# a run of inlined code ended at the cursor and the next begun when the site
# an instruction was inlined at differs from the code's before it
fun state_site(b: *Body, at: Instruction) err[*Error] {
    if (!b.e.stated) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    val site: opt[debug_record.Site] = function.data(b.u.code, at).metadata.site;
    val was:  opt[debug_record.Site] = b.site;
    if (sel site.none && sel was.none) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    if (sel site.some) {
        if (sel was.some) {
            if (site.some == was.some) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
        }
    }
    val here: res[build_state.Label, build_refusal.Refusal] = build_label.anonymous(b.e.b);
    if (sel here.err) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.builder{here.err})}; }
    val placed: err[*Error] = builder(b.e, build_label.define(b.e.b, here.ok));
    if (sel placed.err) { ret placed; }
    val closed: err[*Error] = close_site(b, here.ok);
    if (sel closed.err) { ret closed; }
    b.site = site;
    b.run  = here.ok;
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# the open run of inlined code ended at `end`
fun close_site(b: *Body, end: build_state.Label) err[*Error] {
    val was: opt[debug_record.Site] = b.site;
    if (sel was.none) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    b.site = opt[debug_record.Site].none{};
    ret alloc(b.e, vector.push[records.Run](?b.e.runs, records.Run{site: was.some, start: b.run, end: end}));
}

# a point pending at `l` for a place a branch reads, none for a register reading zero, which holds no secret and which
# the short form of the branch masc may write does not read
fun pend(b: *Body, l: build_state.Label, r: rf.Id) err[*Error] {
    val row: opt[*rf.Register] = rf.row_of(b.e.opened.basis.set.codec.registers, r);
    if (sel row.some) {
        if ((row.some.flags & rf.ZERO) != 0) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    }
    ret alloc(b.e, vector.push[Pending](?b.e.pending, Pending{function: b.u.function, label: l, side: walk.Side.before{}, place: walk.Place.register{r}, end: opt[build_state.Label].none{}}));
}

# a point pending at `l` after a declassifying copy on the place it writes
fun pend_after(b: *Body, l: build_state.Label, place: walk.Place) err[*Error] {
    ret alloc(b.e, vector.push[Pending](?b.e.pending, Pending{function: b.u.function, label: l, side: walk.Side.after{}, place: place, end: opt[build_state.Label].none{}}));
}

# the extent store operand `o` writes, `bits` wide, off its base register: none for an address with an index, a
# segment, a symbol, a base that is no register or a width not of whole bytes
fun stored_extent(o: Operand, bits: u16) opt[walk.Extent] {
    if (!(sel o.address)) { ret opt[walk.Extent].none{}; }
    val a: operand.Address = o.address;
    if (sel a.index.some || sel a.segment.some) { ret opt[walk.Extent].none{}; }
    if (sel a.symbol.some)                      { ret opt[walk.Extent].none{}; }
    if (bits == 0 || bits % 8 != 0)             { ret opt[walk.Extent].none{}; }
    val named: opt[Register] = a.base;
    if (sel named.some) {
        val base: Register = named.some;
        if (sel base.physical) {
            val p: Physical = base.physical;
            if (sel p.register) { ret opt[walk.Extent].some{walk.Extent{base: p.register, offset: a.disp, length: (bits / 8)::u64}}; }
        }
    }
    ret opt[walk.Extent].none{};
}

# a declassifying copy of a function that requires constant time: a label before it, and a point after it on every
# register and extent it writes, each the place it leaves the declassified value in. none is an error
fun declassified_copy(b: *Body, at: Instruction, d: *InstructionData, row: *rows.Row) err[*Error] {
    val l: res[build_state.Label, build_refusal.Refusal] = build_label.anonymous(b.e.b);
    if (sel l.err) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.builder{l.err})}; }
    val placed: err[*Error] = builder(b.e, build_label.define(b.e.b, l.ok));
    if (sel placed.err) { ret placed; }
    val count: u32 = d.operands.size::u32;
    var made:  u32 = 0;
    var n:     u32 = 0;
    for (n < count) {
        val o:      Operand = d.operands.data[n];
        val writes: bool    = (instruction.role(d.opcode, count, n) & mo.WRITE) != 0;
        if (writes) {
            val reg: opt[Physical] = register_of(o);
            if (sel reg.some) {
                val place: Physical = reg.some;
                if (sel place.register) {
                    val pended: err[*Error] = pend_after(b, l.ok, walk.Place.register{place.register});
                    if (sel pended.err) { ret pended; }
                    made = made + 1;
                }
            }
            or (sel o.address) {
                var bits: u16 = 0;
                if (n < row.operands.len) { bits = row.operands.at[n].width; }
                val e: opt[walk.Extent] = stored_extent(o, bits);
                if (sel e.none) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.declassify{site(b, at, n)})}; }
                val pended: err[*Error] = pend_after(b, l.ok, walk.Place.memory{e.some});
                if (sel pended.err) { ret pended; }
                made = made + 1;
            }
        }
        n = n + 1;
    }
    if (made == 0) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.declassify{site(b, at, NO_OPERAND)})}; }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# a declassifying instruction of a function that requires constant time: for a conditional branch a label before it,
# and a point pending there on every register operand and flag it reads, for any other a copy's points
# (`declassified_copy`). a declassifying pseudo-instruction left to emission is an error
fun declassified(b: *Body, at: Instruction) err[*Error] {
    if (!b.timed) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    val d: *InstructionData = function.data(b.u.code, at);
    if (!d.declassifies)     { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    if (!(sel d.opcode.row)) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.declassify{site(b, at, NO_OPERAND)})}; }
    val row: *rows.Row = d.opcode.row;
    if (!row.effect.control.conditional) { ret declassified_copy(b, at, d, row); }
    val l: res[build_state.Label, build_refusal.Refusal] = build_label.anonymous(b.e.b);
    if (sel l.err) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.builder{l.err})}; }
    val placed: err[*Error] = builder(b.e, build_label.define(b.e.b, l.ok));
    if (sel placed.err) { ret placed; }
    val count: u32 = d.operands.size::u32;
    var n:     u32 = 0;
    for (n < count) {
        val reg:   opt[Physical] = register_of(d.operands.data[n]);
        val reads: bool          = (instruction.role(d.opcode, count, n) & mo.READ) != 0;
        if (sel reg.some) {
            val place: Physical = reg.some;
            if (sel place.register) {
                if (reads) {
                    val pended: err[*Error] = pend(b, l.ok, place.register);
                    if (sel pended.err) { ret pended; }
                }
            }
        }
        n = n + 1;
    }
    val file: *rf.File = b.e.opened.basis.set.codec.registers;
    if (file == nil) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    val read: effect.Set = row.effect.flags.read;
    var k:    u32        = 0;
    for (k < file.register_count) {
        if (k / 64 < read.len && ((read.words[k / 64] >> (k % 64)::u64) & 1) != 0) {
            val pended: err[*Error] = pend(b, l.ok, rf.id_of(?file.registers[k]));
            if (sel pended.err) { ret pended; }
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# whether instruction `at` is a call site of the walk: some with whether it is a tail call, a jump to a function, and
# none for any other instruction and for every instruction of a function that does not require constant time
fun calls(b: *Body, at: Instruction) opt[bool] {
    if (!b.timed) { ret opt[bool].none{}; }
    val d: *InstructionData = function.data(b.u.code, at);
    if (!(sel d.opcode.row)) { ret opt[bool].none{}; }
    val got: query.Answer[effect.Control] = instruction.transfer(b.e.opened.basis.set.codec.registers, d);
    if (!(sel got.decided)) { ret opt[bool].none{}; }
    val c: effect.Control = got.decided;
    if (c.transfer == effect.CALL)                                                                     { ret opt[bool].some{false}; }
    if (c.transfer != effect.JUMP || c.target != effect.DIRECT || c.operand::usize >= d.operands.size) { ret opt[bool].none{}; }
    val named: opt[id.Function] = names_function(d.operands.data[c.operand]);
    if (sel named.some) { ret opt[bool].some{true}; }
    ret opt[bool].none{};
}

# the function an operand names, none for one naming none
fun names_function(o: Operand) opt[id.Function] {
    if (sel o.symbol) {
        val s: id.Symbol = o.symbol.symbol;
        if (sel s.function) { ret opt[id.Function].some{s.function}; }
    }
    or (sel o.address) {
        val sym: opt[operand.Symbol] = o.address.symbol;
        if (sel sym.some) {
            val s: id.Symbol = sym.some.symbol;
            if (sel s.function) { ret opt[id.Function].some{s.function}; }
        }
    }
    ret opt[id.Function].none{};
}

# the call site among the `n` instructions of `list` from `k` written as one at label `l`: the first call or tail call
# among them, and the function its own operands name, or else those of an instruction before it its relocation covers
# with it, as risc-v's auipc of a call's pair
fun call_site(b: *Body, list: Slice[Instruction], k: usize, n: usize, l: build_state.Label) err[*Error] {
    var j: usize = 0;
    for (j < n) {
        val at:   Instruction = list.data[k + j];
        val tail: opt[bool]   = calls(b, at);
        if (sel tail.some) {
            var callee: opt[id.Function] = opt[id.Function].none{};
            var s:      usize            = 0;
            for (s <= j && sel callee.none) {
                val d: *InstructionData = function.data(b.u.code, list.data[k + j - s]);
                var o: usize            = 0;
                for (o < d.operands.size && sel callee.none) {
                    callee = names_function(d.operands.data[o]);
                    o      = o + 1;
                }
                s = s + 1;
            }
            ret alloc(b.e, vector.push[Calling](?b.e.calling, Calling{function: b.u.function, label: l, instruction: at, tail: tail.some, callee: callee, steps: n::u32}));
        }
        j = j + 1;
    }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# whether a call site of the walk is among the instructions of `list` from `k` one sequence could cover
fun call_ahead(b: *Body, list: Slice[Instruction], k: usize) bool {
    var j: usize = 0;
    for (j < relax.MAX_STEPS::usize && k + j < list.size) {
        val site: opt[bool] = calls(b, list.data[k + j]);
        if (sel site.some) { ret true; }
        j = j + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# what is stated before an instruction: its range labels, its declassify
# points, its source location, its inlining site and the call frame facts
# before it
fun before(b: *Body, at: Instruction) err[*Error] {
    val marked: err[*Error] = mark_range(b, at);
    if (sel marked.err) { ret marked; }
    val declared: err[*Error] = declassified(b, at);
    if (sel declared.err) { ret declared; }
    val sited: err[*Error] = state_site(b, at);
    if (sel sited.err) { ret sited; }
    val lined: err[*Error] = state_line(b, at);
    if (sel lined.err) { ret lined; }
    ret hand_facts(b, at, false);
}

# the range labels of a block's instructions layout left in no block placed at its end
fun end_block(b: *Body, at: Block) err[*Error] {
    if (b.ends.len == 0) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    val end: opt[build_state.Label] = b.ends.data[at];
    if (sel end.some) {
        val placed: err[*Error] = builder(b.e, build_label.define(b.e.b, end.some));
        if (sel placed.err) { ret placed; }
    }
    val list: *vector.Vector[Range] = ?b.u.ranges.list;
    var i:    usize                 = 0;
    for (i < list.len) {
        val r: *Range = ?list.data[i];
        if (r.block == at) {
            val from: err[*Error] = mark_range(b, r.from);
            if (sel from.err) { ret from; }
        }
        val to: opt[Instruction] = r.to;
        if (r.last == at) {
            if (sel to.some) {
                val ended: err[*Error] = mark_range(b, to.some);
                if (sel ended.err) { ret ended; }
            }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# whether an instruction is a jump table
fun tabled(code: *Function, at: Instruction) bool {
    val op: Opcode = function.data(code, at).opcode;
    ret sel op.pseudo && op.pseudo == pseudo.TABLE;
}

# a jump table met in the code, which emits nothing there: what a range or a
# call frame fact states at it is stated where it stands, after the jump
fun keep_table(b: *Body, at: Instruction) err[*Error] {
    val marked: err[*Error] = mark_range(b, at);
    if (sel marked.err) { ret marked; }
    val before: err[*Error] = hand_facts(b, at, false);
    if (sel before.err) { ret before; }
    val after: err[*Error] = hand_facts(b, at, true);
    if (sel after.err) { ret after; }
    ret alloc(b.e, vector.push[Instruction](?b.tables, at));
}

# the jump tables of a unit laid out, each at its label in the section of a
# constant holding addresses, a section of the unit's own when the build asks
# for code apart, then the unit's section current again
fun lay_tables(b: *Body) err[*Error] {
    if (b.tables.len == 0) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    val e:       *Emitter            = b.e;
    val first:   Instruction         = b.tables.data[0];
    val model:   Addresses           = e.t.addresses;
    val pointer: opt[arches.Pointer] = e.t.arch.pointer;
    if (!(sel model.model)) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.table{site(b, first, NO_OPERAND)})}; }
    if (sel pointer.none)   { ret err[*Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.table{site(b, first, NO_OPERAND)})}; }
    val width:  u64                              = pointer.some.bytes::u64;
    val held:   Contents                         = Contents.addresses{};
    val kind:   *section.Kind                    = address.placement(true, false, held, address.loaded(model.model.relocation, held));
    val placed: res[build_state.Section, *Error] = unit_placed(e, b.u.function, kind, e.apart.code);
    if (sel placed.err) { ret err[*Error].err{placed.err}; }
    val switched: err[*Error] = builder(b.e, build_section.switch(e.b, placed.ok));
    if (sel switched.err) { ret switched; }
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < b.tables.len) {
        val at:   Instruction             = b.tables.data[i];
        val d:    *InstructionData        = function.data(b.u.code, at);
        val mark: opt[*build_state.Label] = map.get[u32, build_state.Label](?b.marks, ?d.label);
        if (sel mark.none) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.label{site(b, at, NO_OPERAND)})}; }
        val aligned: err[*Error] = builder(b.e, build_emit.align(e.b, build_state.Align{boundary: width, fill: opt[u8].none{}, max: opt[u64].none{}}));
        if (sel aligned.err) { ret aligned; }
        val defined: err[*Error] = builder(b.e, build_label.define(e.b, @mark.some));
        if (sel defined.err) { ret defined; }
        var k: usize = 0;
        for (k < d.operands.size) {
            val o: Operand = d.operands.data[k];
            if (!(sel o.block)) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.shape{site(b, at, k::u32)})}; }
            val put: err[*Error] = builder(b.e, build_emit.datum(e.b, build_state.Reference{target: b.blocks.data[o.block], addend: 0, width: width::u8, basis: core_fixup.ABSOLUTE}));
            if (sel put.err) { ret put; }
            k = k + 1;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret builder(b.e, build_section.switch(e.b, b.code));
}

fun emit_body(b: *Body) err[*Error] {
    val code: *Function = b.u.code;
    var i:    usize     = 0;
    for (i < b.u.laid.order.len) {
        val at:     Block              = b.u.laid.order.data[i];
        val list:   Slice[Instruction] = function.instructions(code, at);
        val placed: err[*Error]        = builder(b.e, build_label.define(b.e.b, b.blocks.data[at]));
        if (sel placed.err) { ret placed; }
        var k: usize = 0;
        for (k < list.size) {
            if (tabled(code, list.data[k])) {
                val kept: err[*Error] = keep_table(b, list.data[k]);
                if (sel kept.err) { ret kept; }
                k = k + 1;
                cnt;
            }
            val n: u32 = function.data(code, list.data[k]).label;
            if (n != instruction.NO_LABEL) {
                val mark: opt[*build_state.Label] = map.get[u32, build_state.Label](?b.marks, ?n);
                if (sel mark.none) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.label{site(b, list.data[k], NO_OPERAND)})}; }
                val held: err[*Error] = builder(b.e, build_label.define(b.e.b, @mark.some));
                if (sel held.err) { ret held; }
            }
            val pending: usize       = b.e.pending.len;
            val stated:  err[*Error] = before(b, list.data[k]);
            if (sel stated.err) { ret stated; }
            var site: opt[build_state.Label] = opt[build_state.Label].none{};
            if (b.timed && (call_ahead(b, list, k) || symbolic_ahead(b, list, k) || stated_ahead(b, list, k) || marked_ahead(b, list, k))) {
                val l: res[build_state.Label, build_refusal.Refusal] = build_label.position(b.e.b);
                if (sel l.err) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.builder{l.err})}; }
                site = opt[build_state.Label].some{l.ok};
            }
            val wrote: res[usize, *Error] = write(b, list, k);
            if (sel wrote.err) { ret err[*Error].err{wrote.err}; }
            if (b.e.pending.len > pending) {
                val ended: err[*Error] = end_points(b, list.data[k], pending, wrote.ok);
                if (sel ended.err) { ret ended; }
            }
            # only a unit that requires constant time keeps anything for the walk
            if (b.timed) {
                if (sel site.some) {
                    val sited: err[*Error] = call_site(b, list, k, wrote.ok, site.some);
                    if (sel sited.err) { ret sited; }
                }
                val noted: err[*Error] = fixed(b, list, k, wrote.ok, site);
                if (sel noted.err) { ret noted; }
                val accesses: err[*Error] = accessed(b, list, k, wrote.ok, site);
                if (sel accesses.err) { ret accesses; }
                val secrets: err[*Error] = seeded(b, list, k, wrote.ok, site);
                if (sel secrets.err) { ret secrets; }
                val facts: err[*Error] = marked(b, list, k, wrote.ok, site);
                if (sel facts.err) { ret facts; }
            }
            # what a sequence's later instructions state comes after the sequence, which nothing splits
            var j: usize = 0;
            for (j < wrote.ok) {
                if (j > 0) {
                    val later: err[*Error] = before(b, list.data[k + j]);
                    if (sel later.err) { ret later; }
                }
                val after: err[*Error] = hand_facts(b, list.data[k + j], true);
                if (sel after.err) { ret after; }
                j = j + 1;
            }
            k = k + wrote.ok;
        }
        val ended: err[*Error] = end_block(b, at);
        if (sel ended.err) { ret ended; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# each instruction's call frame facts, in their order
fun index_facts(b: *Body) err[*Error] {
    val code:   *Function            = b.u.code;
    var failed: err[allocator.Error] = slice.fill[u32](?b.facts, code.instructions.len, NONE);
    keep(?failed, slice.fill[u32](?b.next, b.u.facts.size, NONE));
    keep(?failed, slice.fill[bool](?b.given, b.u.facts.size, false));
    if (sel failed.err) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.alloc{failed.err})}; }
    var i: usize = b.u.facts.size;
    for (i > 0) {
        i = i - 1;
        val at: u32 = b.u.facts.data[i].at;
        if (at::usize >= code.instructions.len) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.fact{site(b, b.u.facts.data[i].at, NO_OPERAND)})}; }
        b.next.data[i]   = b.facts.data[at];
        b.facts.data[at] = i::u32;
    }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# a label before each instruction a range begins or ends at, and one at the end of each block a range runs to the end of
fun label_ranges(b: *Body) err[*Error] {
    val r: *Ranges = b.u.ranges;
    if (r == nil)        { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    if (r.list.len == 0) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    val none: err[allocator.Error] = slice.fill[opt[build_state.Label]](?b.ends, b.u.code.blocks.len, opt[build_state.Label].none{});
    if (sel none.err) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.alloc{none.err})}; }
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < r.list.len) {
        val one: *Range = ?r.list.data[i];
        if (!laid_out(b, one.block)) {
            i = i + 1;
            cnt;
        }
        val from: err[*Error] = range_mark(b, one.from, one.block);
        if (sel from.err) { ret from; }
        val to:   opt[Instruction]       = one.to;
        val held: opt[build_state.Label] = b.ends.data[one.last];
        if (sel to.some) {
            val ended: err[*Error] = range_mark(b, to.some, one.last);
            if (sel ended.err) { ret ended; }
        }
        or (sel held.none) {
            val l: res[build_state.Label, build_refusal.Refusal] = build_label.anonymous(b.e.b);
            if (sel l.err) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.builder{l.err})}; }
            b.ends.data[one.last] = opt[build_state.Label].some{l.ok};
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

fun range_mark(b: *Body, at: Instruction, block: u32) err[*Error] {
    if (map.contains[u32, Mark](?b.ranged, ?at)) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    val l: res[build_state.Label, build_refusal.Refusal] = build_label.anonymous(b.e.b);
    if (sel l.err) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.builder{l.err})}; }
    val stored: res[bool, allocator.Error] = map.insert[u32, Mark](?b.ranged, at, Mark{label: l.ok, block: block, defined: false});
    if (sel stored.err) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.alloc{stored.err})}; }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# which blocks layout left in the order it emits and which instructions it
# dropped with their block, the one fate every table at an instruction follows
fun follow_layout(b: *Body) err[*Error] {
    val code:   *Function            = b.u.code;
    var failed: err[allocator.Error] = slice.fill[bool](?b.laid, code.blocks.len, false);
    keep(?failed, slice.fill[bool](?b.gone, code.instructions.len, false));
    if (sel failed.err) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.alloc{failed.err})}; }
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < b.u.laid.order.len) {
        b.laid.data[b.u.laid.order.data[i]] = true;
        i                                   = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < code.blocks.len) {
        if (!b.laid.data[i]) {
            val list: Slice[Instruction] = function.instructions(code, (i::u32));
            var k:    usize              = 0;
            for (k < list.size) {
                b.gone.data[list.data[k]] = true;
                k                         = k + 1;
            }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# whether layout left a block in the order it emits
fun laid_out(b: *Body, k: Block) bool {
    if (k::usize >= b.laid.len) { ret false; }
    ret b.laid.data[k];
}

# whether layout dropped an instruction with its block
fun gone(b: *Body, at: Instruction) bool {
    if (at::usize >= b.gone.len) { ret false; }
    ret b.gone.data[at];
}

# a unit's ranges as the debug records' spans over its labels, those of a
# block layout dropped left out
fun spans_of(b: *Body, end: build_state.Label) err[*Error] {
    val r: *Ranges = b.u.ranges;
    if (r == nil) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < r.list.len) {
        val one: *Range = ?r.list.data[i];
        if (!laid_out(b, one.block)) {
            i = i + 1;
            cnt;
        }
        val from: opt[*Mark] = map.get[u32, Mark](?b.ranged, ?one.from);
        if (sel from.none) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.label{site(b, one.from, NO_OPERAND)})}; }
        var to:   build_state.Label      = end;
        val ends: opt[build_state.Label] = b.ends.data[one.last];
        if (sel ends.some) { to = ends.some; }
        val until: opt[Instruction] = one.to;
        if (sel until.some) {
            val mark: opt[*Mark] = map.get[u32, Mark](?b.ranged, ?until.some);
            if (sel mark.none) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.label{site(b, until.some, NO_OPERAND)})}; }
            to = mark.some.label;
        }
        val pushed: err[*Error] = alloc(b.e, vector.push[records.Span](?b.e.spans, records.Span{binding: one.binding, start: from.some.label, end: to, where: one.where, expression: one.expression, type: one.type}));
        if (sel pushed.err) { ret pushed; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# the label ending each unit's function, made before any function is named so its symbol is exposed once with its range
fun end_units(e: *Emitter, units: Slice[Unit]) err[*Error] {
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < units.size) {
        val f: id.Function = units.data[i].function;
        if (f::usize >= e.emitters.len) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.symbol{module.Error.function{f}})}; }
        val l: res[build_state.Label, build_refusal.Refusal] = build_label.anonymous(e.b);
        if (sel l.err) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.builder{l.err})}; }
        val pushed: err[*Error] = alloc(e, vector.push[build_state.Label](?e.ends, l.ok));
        if (sel pushed.err) { ret pushed; }
        e.emitters.data[f] = opt[u32].some{i::u32};
        i                  = i + 1;
    }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# the section a function's code is placed in: the one it states, else one of its own when the build asks for code
# apart, else the one nameless text section, made current
fun code_section(e: *Emitter, f: id.Function) res[build_state.Section, *Error] {
    val d:      FunctionData = e.m.functions.data[f].data;
    var placed: build_state.Section;
    if (sel d.section.some) {
        val named: res[opt[build_state.Section], *Error] = section_for(e, d.section.some.name, d.section.some.kind);
        if (sel named.err)     { ret res[build_state.Section, *Error].err{named.err}; }
        if (sel named.ok.none) { ret res[build_state.Section, *Error].err{stop(e, Error.section{id.Symbol.function{f}})}; }
        placed = named.ok.some;
    }
    or {
        val kind: res[build_state.Section, *Error] = unit_placed(e, f, ?section.TEXT, e.apart.code);
        if (sel kind.err) { ret kind; }
        placed = kind.ok;
    }
    val switched: err[*Error] = builder(e, build_section.switch(e.b, placed));
    if (sel switched.err) { ret res[build_state.Section, *Error].err{switched.err}; }
    ret res[build_state.Section, *Error].ok{placed};
}

# a nameless section of a kind for a global of linkage `l`, thread-local when `tls`, which states none: for a
# replaceable one, not thread-local, where the format holds weak definitions in a section of their own the section
# masc keeps them in, else as `kind_placed` places it
fun data_placed(e: *Emitter, l: Linkage, tls: bool, kind: *section.Kind) res[build_state.Section, *Error] {
    if (linkage.overridable(l) && !tls) {
        val spec:     build_state.Spec                                     = build_state.Spec{name: opt[str].none{}, kind: kind, flags: kind.flags, disposition: ?section.WHOLE, entsize: 0, apart: true};
        val res_weak: res[opt[build_state.Section], build_refusal.Refusal] = build_section.replaceable(e.b, spec);
        if (sel res_weak.err)     { ret res[build_state.Section, *Error].err{stop(e, Error.builder{res_weak.err})}; }
        if (sel res_weak.ok.some) { ret res[build_state.Section, *Error].ok{res_weak.ok.some}; }
    }
    ret kind_placed(e, kind, e.apart.data);
}

# a nameless section of a kind for part of function `f`, which states none: for a merged function a section of its
# copy (`masc.build.section.copy`), for a replaceable one where the format holds weak definitions in a section of their
# own the section masc keeps them in, else as `kind_placed` places it
fun unit_placed(e: *Emitter, f: id.Function, kind: *section.Kind, apart: bool) res[build_state.Section, *Error] {
    val d:          FunctionData     = e.m.functions.data[f].data;
    val opt_merged: opt[u64]         = d.linkage.merged;
    val spec:       build_state.Spec = build_state.Spec{name: opt[str].none{}, kind: kind, flags: kind.flags, disposition: ?section.WHOLE, entsize: 0, apart: true};
    if (sel opt_merged.some) {
        val res_label: res[build_state.Label, *Error] = function_label(e, f);
        if (sel res_label.err) { ret res[build_state.Section, *Error].err{res_label.err}; }
        val opt_name: opt[View] = build.label_name(e.b, res_label.ok);
        if (sel opt_name.none) { ret res[build_state.Section, *Error].err{stop(e, Error.symbol{module.Error.function{f}})}; }
        val res_made: res[build_state.Section, build_refusal.Refusal] = build_section.copy(e.b, spec, opt_name.some, opt_merged.some);
        if (sel res_made.err) { ret res[build_state.Section, *Error].err{stop(e, Error.builder{res_made.err})}; }
        ret res[build_state.Section, *Error].ok{res_made.ok};
    }
    if (linkage.overridable(d.linkage)) {
        val res_weak: res[opt[build_state.Section], build_refusal.Refusal] = build_section.replaceable(e.b, spec);
        if (sel res_weak.err)     { ret res[build_state.Section, *Error].err{stop(e, Error.builder{res_weak.err})}; }
        if (sel res_weak.ok.some) { ret res[build_state.Section, *Error].ok{res_weak.ok.some}; }
    }
    ret kind_placed(e, kind, apart);
}

# the alignment of a function's entry: the larger of the target's function alignment and the one it states, none
# when neither states one
fun entry_alignment(e: *Emitter, f: id.Function) opt[u64] {
    val stated: opt[u64] = e.m.functions.data[f].data.alignment;
    if (sel stated.none) { ret e.function; }
    if (sel e.function.some) {
        if (e.function.some > stated.some) { ret e.function; }
    }
    ret stated;
}

# one function: its symbol in its section at its alignment, then its blocks, then the label ending it
fun emit_unit(e: *Emitter, u: Unit, end: build_state.Label) err[*Error] {
    if (u.function::usize >= e.m.functions.len) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.symbol{module.Error.function{u.function}})}; }
    val l: res[build_state.Label, *Error] = function_label(e, u.function);
    if (sel l.err) { ret err[*Error].err{l.err}; }
    val code: res[build_state.Section, *Error] = code_section(e, u.function);
    if (sel code.err) { ret err[*Error].err{code.err}; }
    val boundary: opt[u64] = entry_alignment(e, u.function);
    if (sel boundary.some) {
        val aligned: err[*Error] = builder(e, build_emit.align(e.b, build_state.Align{boundary: boundary.some, fill: e.fill, max: opt[u64].none{}}));
        if (sel aligned.err) { ret aligned; }
    }
    val placed: err[*Error] = builder(e, build_label.define(e.b, l.ok));
    if (sel placed.err) { ret placed; }
    # the frame and the debug information describe this definition, which a weak symbol's label need not name once
    # masc makes it a weak external, so they start at a label of its own
    val begin: res[build_state.Label, build_refusal.Refusal] = build_label.anonymous(e.b);
    if (sel begin.err) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.builder{begin.err})}; }
    val begun_at: err[*Error] = builder(e, build_label.define(e.b, begin.ok));
    if (sel begun_at.err) { ret begun_at; }
    val scoped: err[*Error] = builder(e, build_emit.under(e.b, u.context));
    if (sel scoped.err) { ret scoped; }
    val timed: bool = in_constant_time(e.m.functions.data[u.function].data.constant_time);
    if (timed) {
        val begun: err[*Error] = builder(e, frame.ct_begin(e.b));
        if (sel begun.err) { ret begun; }
    }
    var body: Body = Body{
        e:      e,
        u:      u,
        code:   code.ok,
        blocks: vector.init[build_state.Label](e.a),
        marks:  map.init[u32, build_state.Label](e.a),
        facts:  vector.init[u32](e.a),
        next:   vector.init[u32](e.a),
        given:  vector.init[bool](e.a),
        laid:   vector.init[bool](e.a),
        gone:   vector.init[bool](e.a),
        ranged: map.init[u32, Mark](e.a),
        ends:   vector.init[opt[build_state.Label]](e.a),
        site:   opt[debug_record.Site].none{},
        run:    l.ok,
        at:     opt[debug_record.Location].none{},
        spoke:  false,
        tables: vector.init[Instruction](e.a),
        noted:  vector.init[Noted](e.a),
        stated: vector.init[Stated](e.a),
        seeded: vector.init[Declared](e.a),
        uses:   vector.init[masc_inline.Use](e.a),
        steps:  0,
        switch: mct.switching(e.opened.basis.set, u.context),
        timed:  timed,
    };
    fin {
        vector.dnit[build_state.Label](?body.blocks);
        map.dnit[u32, build_state.Label](?body.marks);
        vector.dnit[u32](?body.facts);
        vector.dnit[u32](?body.next);
        vector.dnit[bool](?body.given);
        vector.dnit[bool](?body.laid);
        vector.dnit[bool](?body.gone);
        map.dnit[u32, Mark](?body.ranged);
        vector.dnit[opt[build_state.Label]](?body.ends);
        vector.dnit[Instruction](?body.tables);
        vector.dnit[Noted](?body.noted);
        vector.dnit[Stated](?body.stated);
        vector.dnit[Declared](?body.seeded);
        vector.dnit[masc_inline.Use](?body.uses);
    }
    val followed: err[*Error] = follow_layout(?body);
    if (sel followed.err) { ret followed; }
    val labelled: err[*Error] = label_body(?body);
    if (sel labelled.err) { ret labelled; }
    val indexed: err[*Error] = index_facts(?body);
    if (sel indexed.err) { ret indexed; }
    val ranged: err[*Error] = label_ranges(?body);
    if (sel ranged.err) { ret ranged; }
    if (e.framed) {
        val begun: err[*Error] = builder(e, masc_cfi.start_proc(e.b, begin.ok));
        if (sel begun.err) { ret begun; }
    }
    val spans:   usize       = e.spans.len;
    val runs:    usize       = e.runs.len;
    val emitted: err[*Error] = emit_body(?body);
    if (sel emitted.err) { ret emitted; }
    if (e.framed) {
        var i: usize = 0;
        for (i < u.facts.size) {
            if (!body.given.data[i] && !gone(?body, u.facts.data[i].at)) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.fact{site(?body, u.facts.data[i].at, NO_OPERAND)})}; }
            i = i + 1;
        }
        val ended: err[*Error] = builder(e, masc_cfi.end_proc(e.b));
        if (sel ended.err) { ret ended; }
    }
    val closed: err[*Error] = close_site(?body, end);
    if (sel closed.err) { ret closed; }
    val spanned: err[*Error] = spans_of(?body, end);
    if (sel spanned.err) { ret spanned; }
    val noted: err[*Error] = alloc(e, vector.push[Program](?e.programs, Program{function: u.function, start: begin.ok, end: end, spans: spans, span: e.spans.len - spans, runs: runs, run: e.runs.len - runs}));
    if (sel noted.err) { ret noted; }
    if (timed) {
        val ended: err[*Error] = builder(e, frame.ct_end(e.b));
        if (sel ended.err) { ret ended; }
    }
    val closed_at: err[*Error] = builder(e, build_label.define(e.b, end));
    if (sel closed_at.err) { ret closed_at; }
    val unscoped: err[*Error] = builder(e, build_emit.under(e.b, build_emit.object_of(e.b)));
    if (sel unscoped.err) { ret unscoped; }
    ret lay_tables(?body);
}

fun hash_name(v: *View) u64 {
    ret slice.hash_view(0xcbf29ce484222325, @v);
}

fun same_name(x: *View, y: *View) bool {
    ret slice.same_view(@x, @y);
}

# a kind is its row of mink's catalog, so two kinds are one when they are one row
fun hash_kind(k: **section.Kind) u64 {
    val at: u64 = (@k)::u64;
    ret natural.hash[u64](?at);
}

fun same_kind(x: **section.Kind, y: **section.Kind) bool {
    ret @x == @y;
}

# a new section of a kind, named or nameless, kept apart from every other when `apart` says, and switched to. a
# nameless one, which the target places, is aligned to the target's code or data alignment. a named one is the
# module's placement, so it takes the alignment of what is placed in it, each function at its entry's and each
# global at its own, as a global placed at an offset in a section of its own needs
fun open_section(e: *Emitter, name: opt[str], kind: *section.Kind, apart: bool) res[build_state.Section, *Error] {
    val opened: res[build_state.Section, build_refusal.Refusal] = build_section.open(e.b, build_state.Spec{name: name, kind: kind, flags: kind.flags, disposition: ?section.WHOLE, entsize: 0, apart: apart});
    if (sel opened.err) { ret res[build_state.Section, *Error].err{stop(e, Error.builder{opened.err})}; }
    val switched: err[*Error] = builder(e, build_section.switch(e.b, opened.ok));
    if (sel switched.err) { ret res[build_state.Section, *Error].err{switched.err}; }
    if (sel name.some)    { ret res[build_state.Section, *Error].ok{opened.ok}; }
    var boundary: opt[u64] = align_of(e.t.caps.code.data);
    if ((kind.flags & section.EXEC) != 0) { boundary = align_of(e.t.caps.code.text); }
    if (sel boundary.some) {
        val aligned: err[*Error] = builder(e, build_emit.align(e.b, build_state.Align{boundary: boundary.some, fill: opt[u8].none{}, max: opt[u64].none{}}));
        if (sel aligned.err) { ret res[build_state.Section, *Error].err{aligned.err}; }
    }
    ret res[build_state.Section, *Error].ok{opened.ok};
}

# the section of a name the module states and a kind, opened the first time it is named
# ---
# ret: the section, none when the name is of a section opened with another kind
fun section_for(e: *Emitter, name: View, kind: *section.Kind) res[opt[build_state.Section], *Error] {
    val held: opt[*Opened] = map.get_by[View, Opened](?e.sections, ?name);
    if (sel held.some) {
        if (held.some.kind != kind) { ret res[opt[build_state.Section], *Error].ok{opt[build_state.Section].none{}}; }
        ret res[opt[build_state.Section], *Error].ok{opt[build_state.Section].some{held.some.section}};
    }
    val text: res[*u8, *Error] = terminated(e, name);
    if (sel text.err) { ret res[opt[build_state.Section], *Error].err{text.err}; }
    val opened: res[build_state.Section, *Error] = open_section(e, opt[str].some{text.ok}, kind, false);
    unterminated(e, text.ok, name);
    if (sel opened.err) { ret res[opt[build_state.Section], *Error].err{opened.err}; }
    val stored: res[bool, allocator.Error] = map.insert_by[View, Opened](?e.sections, name, Opened{section: opened.ok, kind: kind});
    if (sel stored.err) { ret res[opt[build_state.Section], *Error].err{stop(e, Error.alloc{stored.err})}; }
    ret res[opt[build_state.Section], *Error].ok{opt[build_state.Section].some{opened.ok}};
}

# the one nameless section of a kind, which mink names as the format names a section of the kind, opened the first
# time the kind is placed with no name the module states
fun kind_section(e: *Emitter, kind: *section.Kind) res[build_state.Section, *Error] {
    val held: opt[*build_state.Section] = map.get_by[*section.Kind, build_state.Section](?e.kinds, ?kind);
    if (sel held.some) { ret res[build_state.Section, *Error].ok{@held.some}; }
    val opened: res[build_state.Section, *Error] = open_section(e, opt[str].none{}, kind, false);
    if (sel opened.err) { ret opened; }
    val stored: res[bool, allocator.Error] = map.insert_by[*section.Kind, build_state.Section](?e.kinds, kind, opened.ok);
    if (sel stored.err) { ret res[build_state.Section, *Error].err{stop(e, Error.alloc{stored.err})}; }
    ret opened;
}

# a nameless section of a kind for a symbol that states none: one of its own, opened apart, when `apart` says, else
# the one the kind's symbols share
fun kind_placed(e: *Emitter, kind: *section.Kind, apart: bool) res[build_state.Section, *Error] {
    if (apart) { ret open_section(e, opt[str].none{}, kind, true); }
    ret kind_section(e, kind);
}

# the section the loader's table entry of function `f` lies in, at priority `run_at`: one of the function's own copy
# where it is merged, so the image keeps one entry with the one copy it keeps, else one apart
fun entry_placed(e: *Emitter, f: id.Function, run_at: u32) res[build_state.Section, *Error] {
    val spec:       build_state.Spec = build_state.Spec{name: opt[str].none{}, kind: ?section.INIT_ARRAY, flags: section.INIT_ARRAY.flags, disposition: ?section.WHOLE, entsize: 0, apart: true, priority: opt[u32].some{run_at}};
    val opt_merged: opt[u64]         = e.m.functions.data[f].data.linkage.merged;
    if (sel opt_merged.some) {
        val res_label: res[build_state.Label, *Error] = function_label(e, f);
        if (sel res_label.err) { ret res[build_state.Section, *Error].err{res_label.err}; }
        val opt_name: opt[View] = build.label_name(e.b, res_label.ok);
        if (sel opt_name.none) { ret res[build_state.Section, *Error].err{stop(e, Error.symbol{module.Error.function{f}})}; }
        val res_copy: res[build_state.Section, build_refusal.Refusal] = build_section.copy(e.b, spec, opt_name.some, opt_merged.some);
        if (sel res_copy.err) { ret res[build_state.Section, *Error].err{stop(e, Error.builder{res_copy.err})}; }
        ret res[build_state.Section, *Error].ok{res_copy.ok};
    }
    val res_open: res[build_state.Section, build_refusal.Refusal] = build_section.open(e.b, spec);
    if (sel res_open.err) { ret res[build_state.Section, *Error].err{stop(e, Error.builder{res_open.err})}; }
    ret res[build_state.Section, *Error].ok{res_open.ok};
}

# the entry of each function of `units` the image's loader runs when it loads the image: the function's address, a
# word of the target's pointer width, in a table of functions the loader runs at the function's priority
fun initialisers(e: *Emitter, units: Slice[Unit]) err[*Error] {
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < units.size) {
        val f: id.Function = units.data[i].function;
        i = i + 1;
        val run_at: opt[u32] = e.m.functions.data[f].data.init;
        if (sel run_at.none) { cnt; }
        val width: opt[u8] = arches.pointer_bytes(e.t.arch);
        if (sel width.none) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.symbol{module.Error.function{f}})}; }
        val placed: res[build_state.Section, *Error] = entry_placed(e, f, run_at.some);
        if (sel placed.err) { ret err[*Error].err{placed.err}; }
        val switched: err[*Error] = builder(e, build_section.switch(e.b, placed.ok));
        if (sel switched.err) { ret switched; }
        val aligned: err[*Error] = builder(e, build_emit.align(e.b, build_state.Align{boundary: width.some::u64, fill: opt[u8].none{}, max: opt[u64].none{}}));
        if (sel aligned.err) { ret aligned; }
        val l: res[build_state.Label, *Error] = address_label(e, f);
        if (sel l.err) { ret err[*Error].err{l.err}; }
        val put: err[*Error] = builder(e, build_emit.datum(e.b, build_state.Reference{target: l.ok, addend: 0, width: width.some, basis: core_fixup.ABSOLUTE}));
        if (sel put.err) { ret put; }
    }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# the bytes of an image from `from` to `to`
fun bytes_of(e: *Emitter, i: *data.Image, from: u64, to: u64) err[*Error] {
    if (to <= from) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    ret builder(e, build_emit.data(e.b, ?i.bytes.data[from::usize], (to - from)::usize));
}

# an initial value's bytes, with a datum for each address in it
fun write_image(e: *Emitter, g: id.Global, i: *data.Image) err[*Error] {
    var at: u64   = 0;
    var k:  usize = 0;
    for (k < i.datums.len) {
        val d: data.Datum = i.datums.data[k];
        if (d.width > core_fixup.MAX_WIDTH::u64) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.width{g})}; }
        val before: err[*Error] = bytes_of(e, i, at, d.offset);
        if (sel before.err) { ret before; }
        val l: res[build_state.Label, *Error] = datum_label(e, d.symbol);
        if (sel l.err) { ret err[*Error].err{l.err}; }
        val put: err[*Error] = builder(e, build_emit.datum(e.b, build_state.Reference{target: l.ok, addend: d.addend, width: d.width::u8, basis: core_fixup.ABSOLUTE}));
        if (sel put.err) { ret put; }
        at = d.offset + d.width;
        k  = k + 1;
    }
    ret bytes_of(e, i, at, i.bytes.len::u64);
}

# one global the module defines: its symbol in its section, its own when the build asks for data apart and it states
# none, at its alignment, then its initial value
fun emit_global(e: *Emitter, g: id.Global) err[*Error] {
    val d: GlobalData = e.m.globals.data[g].data;
    if (sel d.initial.none) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    val held: res[Contents, module.Error] = module.contents(e.m, d.initial.some);
    if (sel held.err) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.contents{Valued{global: g, error: held.err}})}; }
    var placed: build_state.Section;
    if (sel d.section.some) {
        val named: res[opt[build_state.Section], *Error] = section_for(e, d.section.some.name, d.section.some.kind);
        if (sel named.err)     { ret err[*Error].err{named.err}; }
        if (sel named.ok.none) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.section{id.Symbol.global{g}})}; }
        placed = named.ok.some;
    }
    or {
        var relocated: bool = false;
        if (sel held.ok.addresses) {
            val a: Addresses = e.t.addresses;
            if (!(sel a.model)) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.model{g})}; }
            relocated = address.loaded(a.model.relocation, held.ok);
        }
        val kind: res[build_state.Section, *Error] = data_placed(e, d.linkage, sel d.tls.some, address.placement(d.constant, sel d.tls.some, held.ok, relocated));
        if (sel kind.err) { ret err[*Error].err{kind.err}; }
        placed = kind.ok;
    }
    val switched: err[*Error] = builder(e, build_section.switch(e.b, placed));
    if (sel switched.err) { ret switched; }
    val ext: res[Extent, record.Error] = layout.extent(?e.l, d.type, DEFAULT_SPACE);
    if (sel ext.err) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.layout{Sized{global: g, error: ext.err}})}; }
    var boundary: u64 = ext.ok.align;
    if (sel d.alignment.some) { boundary = d.alignment.some; }
    val aligned: err[*Error] = builder(e, build_emit.align(e.b, build_state.Align{boundary: boundary, fill: opt[u8].none{}, max: opt[u64].none{}}));
    if (sel aligned.err) { ret aligned; }
    val l: res[build_state.Label, *Error] = global_label(e, g);
    if (sel l.err) { ret err[*Error].err{l.err}; }
    val defined: err[*Error] = builder(e, build_label.define(e.b, l.ok));
    if (sel defined.err)   { ret defined; }
    if (sel held.ok.zeros) { ret builder(e, build_emit.zero(e.b, ext.ok.size)); }
    val made: res[data.Image, data.Error] = data.image(e.a, e.m, ?e.l, DEFAULT_SPACE, e.order, d.initial.some, ext.ok.size);
    if (sel made.err) {
        val why: data.Error = made.err;
        if (sel why.alloc)  { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.alloc{why.alloc})}; }
        or (sel why.layout) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.layout{Sized{global: g, error: why.layout}})}; }
        val read: module.Error = why.ir;
        ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.contents{Valued{global: g, error: read}})};
    }
    var image: data.Image = made.ok;
    fin { data.release(?image); }
    ret write_image(e, g, ?image);
}

# the byte code is padded with, from the target's declaration
fun fill_of(f: Fill) res[opt[u8], Error] {
    if (sel f.pattern) {
        if (f.pattern.size == 0) { ret res[opt[u8], Error].err{Error.fill{}}; }
        var i: usize = 1;
        for (i < f.pattern.size) {
            if (f.pattern.data[i] != f.pattern.data[0]) { ret res[opt[u8], Error].err{Error.fill{}}; }
            i = i + 1;
        }
        ret res[opt[u8], Error].ok{opt[u8].some{f.pattern.data[0]}};
    }
    ret res[opt[u8], Error].ok{opt[u8].none{}};
}

# the psABI row of mink's catalog the convention is for architecture `arch`, whose traits masc's builder states for
# the object
pub fun abi_of(c: *Convention, arch: *arches.Arch) res[*arches.Abi, Error] {
    val row: res[*arches.Abi, Unadmitted] = convention.abi_row(c, arch);
    if (sel row.err) { ret res[*arches.Abi, Error].err{Error.abi{}}; }
    ret res[*arches.Abi, Error].ok{row.ok};
}

# the alignment a declaration states, none for none
fun align_of(a: Align) opt[u64] {
    if (sel a.bytes) { ret opt[u64].some{a.bytes}; }
    ret opt[u64].none{};
}

# whether masc states the frame the architecture's functions start in, so a function can be a frame of the builder
fun starts_frames(opened: *Build, arch: *arches.Arch) bool {
    val row: opt[*masc_set.Arch] = masc_set.arch_of(opened.basis.set, arch);
    if (sel row.none) { ret false; }
    ret row.some.frame != nil;
}

# every source file of the module stated to masc's line facts in table order, so a file's index is its id's
fun files(e: *Emitter) err[*Error] {
    if (!e.stated) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < e.m.debug.files.len) {
        val named: res[u32, build_refusal.Refusal] = masc_line.file(?e.lines, masc_line.Source{directory: View{data: nil, len: 0}, name: e.m.debug.files.data[i], md5: opt[mink_line.Md5].none{}});
        if (sel named.err) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.builder{named.err})}; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# the debug records of a module that states source files, stated on the object from every unit's spans and runs and
# every global's label, for a format whose lowering writes dwarf information and an architecture of addresses
fun describe(e: *Emitter, o: *object.Object, format: *Format) err[*Error] {
    if (!e.stated) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    val pointer: opt[arches.Pointer] = e.t.arch.pointer;
    if (sel pointer.none) { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    val informed: res[bool, *Error] = informs(e, format);
    if (sel informed.err) { ret err[*Error].err{informed.err}; }
    if (!informed.ok)     { ret err[*Error].ok{}; }
    var programs: vector.Vector[records.Subprogram] = vector.init[records.Subprogram](e.a);
    fin { vector.dnit[records.Subprogram](?programs); }
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < e.programs.len) {
        val p:    Program            = e.programs.data[i];
        val made: records.Subprogram = records.Subprogram{
            function: p.function,
            start:    p.start,
            end:      p.end,
            spans:    Slice[records.Span]{data: ?e.spans.data[p.spans], size: p.span},
            runs:     Slice[records.Run]{data: ?e.runs.data[p.runs], size: p.run},
        };
        val pushed: err[*Error] = alloc(e, vector.push[records.Subprogram](?programs, made));
        if (sel pushed.err) { ret pushed; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    var r: records.Request = records.Request{
        a:         e.a,
        m:         e.m,
        l:         ?e.l,
        b:         e.b,
        context:   ?e.opened.basis.context,
        o:         o,
        functions: Slice[records.Subprogram]{data: programs.data, size: programs.len},
        globals:   Slice[opt[build_state.Label]]{data: e.globals.data, size: e.globals.len},
    };
    val stated: err[records.Error] = records.state(?r);
    if (sel stated.err) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.debug{stated.err})}; }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# whether the object's format lowers debug records to dwarf information, as mink's lowering of it states
fun informs(e: *Emitter, format: *Format) res[bool, *Error] {
    val got: res[*registration.Registration, Fail] = registry.by_format(e.opened.formats, format);
    if (sel got.err) { ret res[bool, *Error].err{stop(e, Error.lowering{got.err})}; }
    val lowering: opt[*mink_lower.Lowering] = registration.lowering(got.ok);
    if (sel lowering.none) { ret res[bool, *Error].ok{false}; }
    ret res[bool, *Error].ok{sel lowering.some.info.some};
}

# the label after declassifying instruction `at`, written alone, on each point pending from `from`, so each point
# states the length of its own instruction. a declassify written in a sequence of `count` is an error
fun end_points(b: *Body, at: Instruction, from: usize, count: usize) err[*Error] {
    if (count != 1) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.declassify{site(b, at, NO_OPERAND)})}; }
    val l: res[build_state.Label, build_refusal.Refusal] = build_label.position(b.e.b);
    if (sel l.err) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(b.e, Error.builder{l.err})}; }
    var i: usize = from;
    for (i < b.e.pending.len) {
        b.e.pending.data[i].end = opt[build_state.Label].some{l.ok};
        i                       = i + 1;
    }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# each pending declassify point, call site, symbolic operand, stated memory access and declared secret, and each line
# fact of a function that requires constant time, at the place its label lies in the finished object
fun resolve(e: *Emitter, out: *timed.Marks) err[*Error] {
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < e.pending.len) {
        val p:  *Pending          = ?e.pending.data[i];
        val at: opt[object.Place] = build.place_of(e.b, p.label);
        if (sel at.none)    { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.symbol{module.Error.function{p.function}})}; }
        if (sel p.end.none) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.symbol{module.Error.function{p.function}})}; }
        val end: opt[object.Place] = build.place_of(e.b, p.end.some);
        if (sel end.none)                      { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.symbol{module.Error.function{p.function}})}; }
        if (end.some.offset <= at.some.offset) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.symbol{module.Error.function{p.function}})}; }
        val pushed: err[*Error] = alloc(e, vector.push[timed.Point](?out.points, timed.Point{function: p.function, at: at.some, length: end.some.offset - at.some.offset, side: p.side, place: p.place}));
        if (sel pushed.err) { ret pushed; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < e.calling.len) {
        val c:  *Calling          = ?e.calling.data[i];
        val at: opt[object.Place] = build.place_of(e.b, c.label);
        if (sel at.none) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.symbol{module.Error.function{c.function}})}; }
        val site:   timed.Site  = timed.Site{function: c.function, at: at.some, instruction: c.instruction, tail: c.tail, callee: c.callee, steps: c.steps};
        val pushed: err[*Error] = alloc(e, vector.push[timed.Site](?out.sites, site));
        if (sel pushed.err) { ret pushed; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < e.fixing.len) {
        val x:  *Fixing           = ?e.fixing.data[i];
        val at: opt[object.Place] = build.place_of(e.b, x.label);
        if (sel at.none) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.symbol{module.Error.function{x.function}})}; }
        var partner: opt[object.Place]      = opt[object.Place].none{};
        val mark:    opt[build_state.Label] = x.partner;
        if (sel mark.some) {
            partner = build.place_of(e.b, mark.some);
            if (sel partner.none) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.symbol{module.Error.function{x.function}})}; }
        }
        val fixup:  timed.Fixup = timed.Fixup{function: x.function, at: at.some, step: x.step, operand: x.operand, fixup: x.fixup, symbol: x.symbol, addend: x.addend, partner: partner};
        val pushed: err[*Error] = alloc(e, vector.push[timed.Fixup](?out.fixups, fixup));
        if (sel pushed.err) { ret pushed; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < e.stating.len) {
        val x:  *Stating          = ?e.stating.data[i];
        val at: opt[object.Place] = build.place_of(e.b, x.label);
        if (sel at.none) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.symbol{module.Error.function{x.function}})}; }
        val access: timed.Stated = timed.Stated{function: x.function, at: at.some, step: x.step, access: x.access, secrecy: x.secrecy, secret: x.secret, extent: x.extent};
        val pushed: err[*Error]  = alloc(e, vector.push[timed.Stated](?out.accesses, access));
        if (sel pushed.err) { ret pushed; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < e.seeding.len) {
        val x:  *Seeding          = ?e.seeding.data[i];
        val at: opt[object.Place] = build.place_of(e.b, x.label);
        if (sel at.none) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.symbol{module.Error.function{x.function}})}; }
        val pushed: err[*Error] = alloc(e, vector.push[timed.Result](?out.results, timed.Result{function: x.function, at: at.some, step: x.step, register: x.register}));
        if (sel pushed.err) { ret pushed; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < e.marking.len) {
        val x:  *Marking          = ?e.marking.data[i];
        val at: opt[object.Place] = build.place_of(e.b, x.label);
        if (sel at.none) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.symbol{module.Error.function{x.function}})}; }
        val pushed: err[*Error] = alloc(e, vector.push[timed.Marked](?out.marked, timed.Marked{function: x.function, at: at.some, step: x.step, fact: x.fact}));
        if (sel pushed.err) { ret pushed; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < e.sourced.len) {
        val s: *Sourced = ?e.sourced.data[i];
        if (timed.requires(e.m, s.function)) {
            val at: opt[object.Place] = build.place_of(e.b, masc_line.mark_at(?e.lines, i).at);
            if (sel at.none) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.symbol{module.Error.function{s.function}})}; }
            val pushed: err[*Error] = alloc(e, vector.push[timed.Line](?out.lines, timed.Line{function: s.function, at: at.some, location: s.location}));
            if (sel pushed.err) { ret pushed; }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# give each function and global the module marks exported its symbol of the object, as one no unit or operand named
# has none yet
fun label_exported(e: *Emitter) err[*Error] {
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < e.m.functions.len) {
        if (e.m.functions.data[i].data.linkage.export) {
            val l: res[build_state.Label, *Error] = function_label(e, (i::u32));
            if (sel l.err) { ret err[*Error].err{l.err}; }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < e.m.globals.len) {
        if (e.m.globals.data[i].data.linkage.export) {
            val l: res[build_state.Label, *Error] = global_label(e, (i::u32));
            if (sel l.err) { ret err[*Error].err{l.err}; }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# an export directive on the finished object `o` for each function and global the module marks exported
fun export_all(e: *Emitter, o: *object.Object) err[*Error] {
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < e.m.functions.len) {
        if (e.m.functions.data[i].data.linkage.export) {
            val stated: err[*Error] = export_one(e, o, id.Symbol.function{(i::u32)}, e.functions.data[i]);
            if (sel stated.err) { ret stated; }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < e.m.globals.len) {
        if (e.m.globals.data[i].data.linkage.export) {
            val stated: err[*Error] = export_one(e, o, id.Symbol.global{(i::u32)}, e.globals.data[i]);
            if (sel stated.err) { ret stated; }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# the export directive of `s`, whose label is `l`: about the symbol of the object the label became, exporting it by
# that symbol's name, stating no attribute of a pe export, as mink takes code or data from the symbol's kind
fun export_one(e: *Emitter, o: *object.Object, s: id.Symbol, l: opt[build_state.Label]) err[*Error] {
    var held: opt[mink_table.Id[object.Symbol]] = opt[mink_table.Id[object.Symbol]].none{};
    if (sel l.some)    { held = build.symbol_of(e.b, l.some); }
    if (sel held.none) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.export{Unexported{symbol: s, failure: opt[Fail].none{}}})}; }
    val name:  mink_table.Id[Name]                        = object.symbol_at(o, held.some).name;
    val plain: directive.Export                           = directive.Export{ordinal: opt[u16].none{}, noname: false, private: false, forward: opt[mink_table.Id[Name]].none{}, data: false};
    val added: res[mink_table.Id[object.Directive], Fail] = object.add_directive(o, object.Directive{kind: ?directive.EXPORT, text: name, symbol: opt[mink_table.Id[Name]].some{name}, export: plain});
    if (sel added.err) { ret err[*Error].err{stop(e, Error.export{Unexported{symbol: s, failure: opt[Fail].some{added.err}}})}; }
    ret err[*Error].ok{};
}

# hand the functions and globals of a module over to masc and take the object it makes
# ---
# a:       the allocator the object and everything made on the way take, the object's the caller's
# m:       the module, whose globals it defines and whose symbols the functions' operands name
# opened:  the target's build
# t:       the target, whose code declaration the alignment and fill come from, and whose layout and addresses place the globals
# units:   the functions, each allocated, framed and laid out
# modes:   the settings of the set's assembler modes the code is written under,
#          every other mode at its initial value
# shorts:  the rows an instruction is handed over in once its registers are allocated, in place of its own
# apart:   which symbols the build asks to place each in a section of its own
# listing: where masc's listing of the object is appended in the set's default syntax, none for no listing
# marks:   where the declassify points and call sites of the code are appended, each at its place in the object, none
#          for no walk
# sink:    where masc's layout and encode times and instruction count are kept, none for none
# name:    the object's name, no other object's in a link it is linked in
# ret:     mink's object in memory, or why it was not made, leaving nothing
pub fun emit(a: *allocator.Allocator, m: *Module, opened: *Build, t: *Target, units: Slice[Unit], modes: Slice[mode.Setting], shorts: Shorts, apart: Apart, listing: opt[*vector.Vector[u8]], marks: opt[*timed.Marks], sink: opt[*Stats], name: str) res[object.Object, Error] {
    val arch: *arches.Arch                 = t.arch;
    val row:  res[*Convention, call.Error] = call.of(t);
    if (sel row.err) { ret res[object.Object, Error].err{Error.convention{row.err}}; }
    val abi: res[*arches.Abi, Error] = abi_of(row.ok, arch);
    if (sel abi.err) { ret res[object.Object, Error].err{abi.err}; }
    val format: *Format             = record.format(t);
    val fill:   res[opt[u8], Error] = fill_of(t.caps.code.fill);
    if (sel fill.err) { ret res[object.Object, Error].err{fill.err}; }
    val indexed: res[fixup.Index, allocator.Error] = fixup.make(a, opened.basis.set, arch);
    if (sel indexed.err) { ret res[object.Object, Error].err{Error.alloc{indexed.err}}; }
    var x: fixup.Index = indexed.ok;
    fin { fixup.release(?x); }
    val made: res[build_state.Builder, build_refusal.Refusal] = build.make_named(a, opened.formats, opened.basis.set, ?opened.basis.context, arch, format, module.lend(m));
    if (sel made.err) {
        module.spent(m);
        ret res[object.Object, Error].err{Error.builder{made.err}};
    }
    var b:     build_state.Builder = made.ok;
    var taken: bool                = false;
    module.lent_to(m, ?build.output(?b).names);
    fin {
        if (taken) { module.spent(m); }
        or         { module.take_back(m, build.output(?b)); }
        build.release(?b);
    }
    if (sel sink.some) { build.measure(?b, ?sink.some.masc); }
    val called: err[build_refusal.Refusal] = build.name_object(?b, View{data: name, len: str_len(name)});
    if (sel called.err) { ret res[object.Object, Error].err{Error.builder{called.err}}; }
    val named: err[build_refusal.Refusal] = trait.traits(?b, abi.ok);
    if (sel named.err) { ret res[object.Object, Error].err{Error.builder{named.err}}; }
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < modes.size) {
        val set: err[build_refusal.Refusal] = build.set_mode(?b, modes.data[k]);
        if (sel set.err) { ret res[object.Object, Error].err{Error.builder{set.err}}; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    var e: Emitter = Emitter{
        a:         a,
        m:         m,
        opened:    opened,
        t:         t,
        l:         layout.of(t, ?m.types, opt[*core_state.Context].some{?opened.basis.context}),
        order:     arch.order,
        b:         ?b,
        x:         ?x,
        functions: vector.init[opt[build_state.Label]](a),
        ends:      vector.init[build_state.Label](a),
        emitters:  vector.init[opt[u32]](a),
        globals:   vector.init[opt[build_state.Label]](a),
        sections:  map.init_by[View, Opened](a, hash_name, same_name),
        kinds:     map.init_by[*section.Kind, build_state.Section](a, hash_kind, same_kind),
        apart:     apart,
        fill:      fill.ok,
        function:  align_of(t.caps.code.function),
        framed:    starts_frames(opened, arch),
        lines:     masc_line.make(a),
        stated:    m.debug.files.len > 0,
        sourced:   vector.init[Sourced](a),
        spans:     vector.init[records.Span](a),
        runs:      vector.init[records.Run](a),
        programs:  vector.init[Program](a),
        named:     vector.init[build_state.Label](a),
        pending:   vector.init[Pending](a),
        calling:   vector.init[Calling](a),
        fixing:    vector.init[Fixing](a),
        stating:   vector.init[Stating](a),
        seeding:   vector.init[Seeding](a),
        marking:   vector.init[Marking](a),
        shorts:    shorts,
        bridging:  row.ok.bridging,
        default:   row.ok,
        routine:   convention.probe_helper(row.ok),
        plain:     vector.init[opt[build_state.Label]](a),
    };
    fin {
        vector.dnit[opt[build_state.Label]](?e.functions);
        vector.dnit[build_state.Label](?e.ends);
        vector.dnit[opt[u32]](?e.emitters);
        vector.dnit[opt[build_state.Label]](?e.globals);
        map.dnit_by[View, Opened](?e.sections);
        map.dnit_by[*section.Kind, build_state.Section](?e.kinds);
        masc_line.release(?e.lines);
        vector.dnit[Sourced](?e.sourced);
        vector.dnit[records.Span](?e.spans);
        vector.dnit[records.Run](?e.runs);
        vector.dnit[Program](?e.programs);
        vector.dnit[build_state.Label](?e.named);
        vector.dnit[Pending](?e.pending);
        vector.dnit[Calling](?e.calling);
        vector.dnit[Fixing](?e.fixing);
        vector.dnit[Stating](?e.stating);
        vector.dnit[Seeding](?e.seeding);
        vector.dnit[Marking](?e.marking);
        vector.dnit[opt[build_state.Label]](?e.plain);
    }
    val sourced: err[*Error] = files(?e);
    if (sel sourced.err) { ret res[object.Object, Error].err{@sourced.err}; }
    val unnamed: err[allocator.Error] = slice.fill[opt[build_state.Label]](?e.functions, m.functions.len, opt[build_state.Label].none{});
    if (sel unnamed.err) { ret res[object.Object, Error].err{Error.alloc{unnamed.err}}; }
    val unspelled: err[allocator.Error] = slice.fill[opt[build_state.Label]](?e.plain, m.functions.len, opt[build_state.Label].none{});
    if (sel unspelled.err) { ret res[object.Object, Error].err{Error.alloc{unspelled.err}}; }
    val unemitted: err[allocator.Error] = slice.fill[opt[u32]](?e.emitters, m.functions.len, opt[u32].none{});
    if (sel unemitted.err) { ret res[object.Object, Error].err{Error.alloc{unemitted.err}}; }
    val ended: err[*Error] = end_units(?e, units);
    if (sel ended.err) { ret res[object.Object, Error].err{@ended.err}; }
    val unplaced: err[allocator.Error] = slice.fill[opt[build_state.Label]](?e.globals, m.globals.len, opt[build_state.Label].none{});
    if (sel unplaced.err) { ret res[object.Object, Error].err{Error.alloc{unplaced.err}}; }
    val text: res[build_state.Section, *Error] = kind_section(?e, ?section.TEXT);
    if (sel text.err) { ret res[object.Object, Error].err{@text.err}; }
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < units.size) {
        val done: err[*Error] = emit_unit(?e, units.data[i], e.ends.data[i]);
        if (sel done.err) { ret res[object.Object, Error].err{@done.err}; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < m.globals.len) {
        val done: err[*Error] = emit_global(?e, (i::u32));
        if (sel done.err) { ret res[object.Object, Error].err{@done.err}; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    val entered: err[*Error] = initialisers(?e, units);
    if (sel entered.err) { ret res[object.Object, Error].err{@entered.err}; }
    val declared: err[*Error] = declare_named(?e);
    if (sel declared.err) { ret res[object.Object, Error].err{@declared.err}; }
    val labelled: err[*Error] = label_exported(?e);
    if (sel labelled.err) { ret res[object.Object, Error].err{@labelled.err}; }
    val bridged: err[*Error] = bridges(?e);
    if (sel bridged.err) { ret res[object.Object, Error].err{@bridged.err}; }
    val finished: res[*object.Object, build_refusal.Refusal] = build.finish(?b);
    if (sel finished.err) { ret res[object.Object, Error].err{finish_refused(?e, finished.err)}; }
    val o:        *object.Object = finished.ok;
    val exported: err[*Error]    = export_all(?e, o);
    if (sel exported.err) { ret res[object.Object, Error].err{@exported.err}; }
    val described: err[*Error] = describe(?e, o, format);
    if (sel described.err) { ret res[object.Object, Error].err{@described.err}; }
    if (sel marks.some) {
        val resolved: err[*Error] = resolve(?e, marks.some);
        if (sel resolved.err) { ret res[object.Object, Error].err{@resolved.err}; }
    }
    if (sel listing.some) {
        val dialect: opt[*masc_dialect.Dialect] = masc_dialect.of(format, arch);
        if (sel dialect.none) { ret res[object.Object, Error].err{Error.dialect{format}}; }
        val listed: err[masc_listing.Refusal] = masc_listing.write(?b, masc_listing.Options{syntax: masc_listing.DEFAULT, dialect: dialect.some}, listing.some);
        if (sel listed.err) { ret res[object.Object, Error].err{unlisted(?e, listed.err)}; }
    }
    val handed: res[object.Object, build_refusal.Refusal] = build.take(?b);
    if (sel handed.err) { ret res[object.Object, Error].err{Error.builder{handed.err}}; }
    taken = true;
    ret res[object.Object, Error].ok{handed.ok};
}
